1
00:00:02,327 --> 00:00:05,397
(The Room of Time opens on day one.)

2
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:13,344
(Na Young enters the room first.)

3
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:22,647
(Startled)

4
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:23,715
No way.

5
00:00:24,583 --> 00:00:25,717
What's this?

6
00:00:27,686 --> 00:00:30,522
"Give your 100 minutes
to someone you like."

7
00:00:30,522 --> 00:00:32,858
"Choose at least one person."

8
00:00:32,858 --> 00:00:36,428
(If their combined time is
at least 100 minutes,)

9
00:00:36,428 --> 00:00:38,997
(they will go on a date.)

10
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:40,232
What?

11
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:45,804
(Ten empty slots)

12
00:00:45,804 --> 00:00:49,574
(Ten pieces lie before them.)

13
00:00:50,042 --> 00:00:53,812
(A space for Na Young to fill)

14
00:00:54,746 --> 00:00:57,182
(Thinking)

15
00:01:00,385 --> 00:01:01,553
(Hesitating)

16
00:01:03,155 --> 00:01:06,425
It represented time, but seeing numbers...

17
00:01:06,425 --> 00:01:10,428
made it feel like a measure of affection.

18
00:01:10,429 --> 00:01:12,964
Since it was the first day,

19
00:01:12,964 --> 00:01:15,033
Seon Ho made the best first impression.

20
00:01:23,075 --> 00:01:26,745
(She adds time beside Seon Ho's name.)

21
00:01:26,745 --> 00:01:27,746
For me,

22
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,048
what surprised me most was...

23
00:01:30,682 --> 00:01:31,648
(Reading the battle-against-illness
diaries)

24
00:01:31,649 --> 00:01:32,918
I'll read mine.

25
00:01:33,952 --> 00:01:36,822
While serving in the military,

26
00:01:36,822 --> 00:01:39,524
I was diagnosed with stage four cancer.

27
00:01:40,993 --> 00:01:42,828
How did he endure that?

28
00:01:42,828 --> 00:01:44,296
Seriously,

29
00:01:44,296 --> 00:01:45,464
that's incredible.

30
00:01:45,464 --> 00:01:46,598
He's amazing.

31
00:01:46,598 --> 00:01:48,300
Yet he looks so healthy.

32
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:49,534
And...

33
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:52,671
I was also curious about Do Gon.

34
00:01:53,305 --> 00:01:56,141
He seemed so resilient at first.

35
00:01:56,141 --> 00:01:58,977
But he also showed a tender side.

36
00:01:58,977 --> 00:02:00,746
He must have had such a hard time.

37
00:02:03,315 --> 00:02:05,550
I wanted to talk to him.

38
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:06,518
I'm curious about him.

39
00:02:06,518 --> 00:02:09,488
(Na Young grew curious about Do Gon.)

40
00:02:16,895 --> 00:02:19,531
(Kim Na Young - 40 minutes - Han Do Gon)

41
00:02:21,366 --> 00:02:23,301
But when I thought about it,

42
00:02:23,301 --> 00:02:25,637
I wanted to talk to the other two too.

43
00:02:25,637 --> 00:02:27,506
(Na Young - 10 minutes - Ryun Gi)

44
00:02:27,506 --> 00:02:29,408
(Na Young - 10 minutes - Jong Eun)

45
00:02:30,175 --> 00:02:32,844
(Na Young - 40 minutes - Seon Ho)

46
00:02:33,712 --> 00:02:37,783
(She sent time to all four men.)

47
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,385
There are ten pieces.

48
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:43,522
Wait.

49
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,325
Can I give all 100 minutes to one person?

50
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:50,529
(Thinking)

51
00:02:52,597 --> 00:02:54,333
I don't think I gave it much thought.

52
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:59,071
When she first walked in,

53
00:02:59,071 --> 00:03:02,741
Ro Bin caught my eye.

54
00:03:03,275 --> 00:03:07,946
She was the opposite of someone fragile.

55
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:10,582
Once I overcome all that,

56
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:13,518
I'm no longer a weak person.

57
00:03:15,354 --> 00:03:19,291
It made me think about...

58
00:03:20,092 --> 00:03:21,693
how resilient she must be.

59
00:03:21,693 --> 00:03:23,528
I became even more curious.

60
00:03:25,664 --> 00:03:29,534
Once someone caught my interest,

61
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:33,105
I gave her all 100 minutes at once.

62
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:35,741
(Jung Yong Hwa)

63
00:03:36,475 --> 00:03:37,976
(Surprised)

64
00:03:37,976 --> 00:03:39,444
There it is.

65
00:03:39,444 --> 00:03:41,313
He went all in.

66
00:03:41,313 --> 00:03:42,581
Goodness, Do Gon.

67
00:03:42,581 --> 00:03:43,615
DGD.

68
00:03:44,282 --> 00:03:45,450
"Direct Guy Do Gon?"

69
00:03:45,817 --> 00:03:47,319
Direct Guy Do Gon.

70
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,954
I love it.

71
00:03:48,954 --> 00:03:52,758
The amount of time they choose...

72
00:03:52,758 --> 00:03:54,559
in the Room of Time...

73
00:03:54,559 --> 00:03:56,261
seems to reveal...

74
00:03:56,261 --> 00:03:59,031
their personality and dating style.

75
00:03:59,031 --> 00:03:59,898
Exactly.

76
00:03:59,898 --> 00:04:01,033
They have a match.

77
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:02,567
Their match is confirmed.

78
00:04:02,567 --> 00:04:04,202
(Do Gon and Ro Bin's first date is set.)

79
00:04:08,507 --> 00:04:13,845
(100 minutes,
Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon matched.)

80
00:04:17,149 --> 00:04:18,483
Since it was the first day,

81
00:04:18,483 --> 00:04:20,585
I thought I should talk to them more.

82
00:04:21,119 --> 00:04:22,988
It isn't that...

83
00:04:22,988 --> 00:04:25,057
I had no interest in any of them.

84
00:04:25,057 --> 00:04:27,959
They all seemed so kind.

85
00:04:27,959 --> 00:04:30,629
I could tell they were good people.

86
00:04:34,066 --> 00:04:35,367
I was curious...

87
00:04:35,367 --> 00:04:37,502
about each of them.

88
00:04:42,841 --> 00:04:48,280
(She divides her time based on curiosity.)

89
00:04:52,184 --> 00:04:58,156
(110 minutes,
Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon matched.)

90
00:04:58,623 --> 00:05:02,027
(Jong Eun enters the Room of Time.)

91
00:05:05,097 --> 00:05:08,900
I thought Min Young was very charming.

92
00:05:15,841 --> 00:05:20,512
(He assigns time to Min Young.)

93
00:05:21,313 --> 00:05:23,615
(And...)

94
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:26,618
Ye Ji and I were both...

95
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:30,155
I was also diagnosed
with acute myeloid leukemia.

96
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:34,092
I thought we might relate to each other.

97
00:05:34,092 --> 00:05:36,395
I wanted to get to know her more.

98
00:05:43,035 --> 00:05:45,804
(Jong Eun - 50 minutes - Min Young)

99
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:48,607
(Jong Eun - 50 minutes - Ye Ji)

100
00:05:51,943 --> 00:05:55,447
(Who will receive Min Young's time?)

101
00:05:59,184 --> 00:06:03,155
I think Seon Ho is the handsome potato.

102
00:06:04,156 --> 00:06:06,658
I wanted to talk to Seon Ho.

103
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:07,626
(Someone she had wondered about)

104
00:06:07,626 --> 00:06:09,895
I wanted to get to know him better.

105
00:06:14,232 --> 00:06:16,168
(Min Young - 40 minutes - Ryun Gi)

106
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:18,136
(Min Young - 60 minutes - Seon Ho)

107
00:06:19,538 --> 00:06:22,641
(Will Min Young's feelings reach Seon Ho?)

108
00:06:32,617 --> 00:06:35,187
Ro Bin made the best first impression.

109
00:06:36,655 --> 00:06:38,256
Those little moments...

110
00:06:38,256 --> 00:06:40,492
made me feel something I hadn't in ages.

111
00:06:41,727 --> 00:06:42,861
(Ryun Gi sends his time to Ro Bin.)

112
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:44,096
I think my heart fluttered a little.

113
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:47,065
He's giving her all of it.

114
00:06:47,065 --> 00:06:47,966
DGR?

115
00:06:47,966 --> 00:06:50,402
Wait, DGR.

116
00:06:50,402 --> 00:06:51,970
(Will Ryun Gi follow Do Gon
and make a bold move?)

117
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:53,138
No.

118
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:01,646
(His last ten minutes went to Na Young.)

119
00:07:03,582 --> 00:07:09,287
(100 minutes,
Seo Ro Bin and Kim Ryun Gi matched.)

120
00:07:13,992 --> 00:07:16,428
The person I met first today,

121
00:07:16,428 --> 00:07:17,396
Seon Ho.

122
00:07:19,498 --> 00:07:21,533
(Heart pounding)

123
00:07:22,534 --> 00:07:24,503
That moment still...

124
00:07:24,503 --> 00:07:26,938
left a very strong impression on me.

125
00:07:31,977 --> 00:07:36,114
(A choice filled with the first spark)

126
00:07:37,783 --> 00:07:40,886
And Do Gon...

127
00:07:40,886 --> 00:07:44,423
was cheerful yet serious.

128
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:47,659
He also seemed considerate.

129
00:07:47,659 --> 00:07:48,927
I was curious about him.

130
00:07:52,631 --> 00:07:56,101
(She sends time to Do Gon too.)

131
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:02,107
(Ye Ji - 50 minutes - Seon Ho)

132
00:08:02,107 --> 00:08:05,444
(Ye Ji - 50 minutes - Do Gon)

133
00:08:08,547 --> 00:08:14,586
(The last person enters the room.)

134
00:08:14,853 --> 00:08:15,854
Here it comes.

135
00:08:17,055 --> 00:08:19,891
I've been dying to know.

136
00:08:19,891 --> 00:08:21,259
Who is it?

137
00:08:22,094 --> 00:08:23,128
Just tell us.

138
00:08:35,007 --> 00:08:37,242
(Sighing)

139
00:08:47,219 --> 00:08:48,820
Was it Ro Bin?

140
00:08:50,088 --> 00:08:51,256
Goodness.

141
00:08:51,256 --> 00:08:52,958
How would he know?

142
00:08:52,958 --> 00:08:54,026
How does he know her?

143
00:08:54,026 --> 00:08:55,260
He knows Ro Bin?

144
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,328
It does seem like Ro Bin, right?

145
00:08:56,328 --> 00:08:58,030
- It isn't Ro Bin.
- No?

146
00:08:58,497 --> 00:08:59,931
(Watching closely)

147
00:09:03,235 --> 00:09:07,806
(Seon Ho pauses on Ro Bin's name.)

148
00:09:09,274 --> 00:09:10,208
But actually...

149
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,344
Can I say this?

150
00:09:13,912 --> 00:09:15,814
I actually know that person.

151
00:09:17,115 --> 00:09:19,951
I thought it was the person I had in mind.

152
00:09:20,952 --> 00:09:22,354
Who is it?

153
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:24,089
Tell us who it is.

154
00:09:24,089 --> 00:09:25,090
(Curious)

155
00:09:25,323 --> 00:09:26,858
My gosh.

156
00:09:27,993 --> 00:09:28,827
Wait a minute.

157
00:09:28,827 --> 00:09:30,228
You're loving this.

158
00:09:32,831 --> 00:09:34,232
(Bouncing with excitement)

159
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:40,305
(Someone Seon Ho never forgot)

160
00:09:50,349 --> 00:09:54,086
(He fills in time for that person.)

161
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:08,000
(Jung Ye Ji)

162
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,134
What?

163
00:10:10,902 --> 00:10:12,137
(Startled)

164
00:10:12,137 --> 00:10:13,972
(Frozen)

165
00:10:13,972 --> 00:10:16,108
- Unbelievable.
- It was Ye Ji.

166
00:10:16,108 --> 00:10:17,042
The first ones.

167
00:10:17,042 --> 00:10:19,211
They were the first ones to meet, right?

168
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:22,547
- Unbelievable.
- Right?

169
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:26,852
(During the first meetings,)

170
00:10:28,587 --> 00:10:32,724
(they were the first to meet each other.)

171
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:40,699
This is so fascinating.

172
00:10:40,699 --> 00:10:43,402
What is Seon Ho and Ye Ji's connection?

173
00:10:43,402 --> 00:10:44,670
I'm so curious.

174
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:47,105
What was their relationship?

175
00:10:47,105 --> 00:10:49,675
But Ye Ji doesn't seem to remember him.

176
00:10:49,675 --> 00:10:51,209
I don't think she does.

177
00:10:51,209 --> 00:10:53,245
It seems only Seon Ho remembers.

178
00:10:53,246 --> 00:10:55,781
- I'm so curious.
- I want to know their relationship.

179
00:10:55,781 --> 00:10:56,882
What was their relationship?

180
00:10:56,882 --> 00:10:58,784
"I think it's her."

181
00:10:58,784 --> 00:11:00,052
He said he knew this person.

182
00:11:00,052 --> 00:11:01,687
- Right.
- Those were his exact words.

183
00:11:02,054 --> 00:11:03,488
He said he knew that person.

184
00:11:03,488 --> 00:11:05,157
I'm curious.

185
00:11:07,159 --> 00:11:12,931
(100 minutes,
Jung Ye Ji and Kim Seon Ho matched.)

186
00:11:13,532 --> 00:11:17,803
(When did their connection begin?)

187
00:11:19,271 --> 00:11:22,374
(Day 1 ends.)

188
00:11:27,045 --> 00:11:30,115
(Yongsan District, Seoul)

189
00:11:31,049 --> 00:11:34,486
(Seon Ho waits for someone.)

190
00:11:34,953 --> 00:11:35,921
It felt strange.

191
00:11:36,788 --> 00:11:38,824
It was my first date after moving in.

192
00:11:38,824 --> 00:11:40,525
It was hard to put into words.

193
00:11:43,028 --> 00:11:46,431
I think it was a new feeling for me.

194
00:11:47,532 --> 00:11:53,138
(He nervously waits for his first date.)

195
00:11:58,243 --> 00:12:02,781
I had no idea who my date was.

196
00:12:02,781 --> 00:12:07,119
I kept wondering who it could be.

197
00:12:07,119 --> 00:12:09,187
Since it was my first date,

198
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:11,590
I was incredibly excited.

199
00:12:24,202 --> 00:12:27,305
There were many people at the bus stop,

200
00:12:27,305 --> 00:12:29,074
but he was the only person I saw.

201
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:34,346
As I got closer,
I realized it was Seon Ho.

202
00:12:35,447 --> 00:12:38,250
That moment remains vivid in my memory.

203
00:12:40,619 --> 00:12:41,486
Hello.

204
00:12:41,953 --> 00:12:43,055
(Bowing)

205
00:12:45,190 --> 00:12:47,392
Hello.

206
00:12:49,094 --> 00:12:49,861
Hello.

207
00:12:49,861 --> 00:12:52,464
(Shy)

208
00:12:52,931 --> 00:12:54,232
Where are we going?

209
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:56,201
We need to go over there.

210
00:12:57,035 --> 00:12:58,236
Are you all right?

211
00:13:03,472 --> 00:13:05,143
(Heart fluttering)

212
00:13:05,143 --> 00:13:07,879
It may be early, but they look great.

213
00:13:08,513 --> 00:13:09,448
They really do.

214
00:13:09,448 --> 00:13:11,316
- I have a good feeling.
- Exactly.

215
00:13:11,316 --> 00:13:12,584
These two...

216
00:13:12,584 --> 00:13:16,121
don't know how much time each gave.

217
00:13:16,121 --> 00:13:18,023
Only we know.

218
00:13:20,325 --> 00:13:25,097
(The date lasts for their combined time.)

219
00:13:25,897 --> 00:13:27,199
Watch out.

220
00:13:29,601 --> 00:13:31,103
- Is this it?
- Yes.

221
00:13:32,170 --> 00:13:33,071
Cool.

222
00:13:34,206 --> 00:13:39,144
(Seon Ho leads her to their first stop.)

223
00:13:42,114 --> 00:13:43,482
What's best here?

224
00:13:43,482 --> 00:13:46,351
We have gelato and wine.
Would you like gelato?

225
00:13:46,351 --> 00:13:48,453
Yes. I heard the gelato here is famous.

226
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:51,189
Really? Then let's try it.

227
00:13:51,189 --> 00:13:52,257
Do you eat mint?

228
00:13:52,257 --> 00:13:55,327
Yes, I'm not picky. Mint is fine.

229
00:13:55,327 --> 00:13:57,496
Then how about grape mint?

230
00:13:58,063 --> 00:14:00,332
One grape mint and one yogurt, please.

231
00:14:00,332 --> 00:14:02,200
Would you like both flavors in one cup?

232
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,368
Yes, please.

233
00:14:04,102 --> 00:14:05,604
It looks delicious.

234
00:14:05,604 --> 00:14:07,372
(Laughing)

235
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:09,408
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

236
00:14:10,175 --> 00:14:12,010
- Would you like to sit outside?
- Yes.

237
00:14:13,245 --> 00:14:18,283
(They sit outside in the warm weather.)

238
00:14:20,886 --> 00:14:22,020
Try some.

239
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:26,124
- Is it good?
- It's delicious.

240
00:14:26,124 --> 00:14:28,727
- The yogurt?
- No, I tried this one.

241
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,728
(Surprised)

242
00:14:29,728 --> 00:14:30,762
Is it good?

243
00:14:31,797 --> 00:14:32,664
It's delicious.

244
00:14:35,367 --> 00:14:37,836
Do you like cold treats like ice cream?

245
00:14:38,537 --> 00:14:39,871
(Bursts out laughing)

246
00:14:39,871 --> 00:14:41,640
- Why?
- That dialect.

247
00:14:42,474 --> 00:14:44,443
I heard myself say that and...

248
00:14:44,843 --> 00:14:47,579
Sometimes, you just can't help it.

249
00:14:47,579 --> 00:14:48,714
You just can't.

250
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:50,949
(Laughing)

251
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:57,489
(Chuckling)

252
00:14:58,724 --> 00:15:00,659
I really thought we wouldn't get matched.

253
00:15:00,892 --> 00:15:02,094
Why?

254
00:15:02,828 --> 00:15:04,162
It just seemed...

255
00:15:04,162 --> 00:15:06,164
like we hadn't really connected.

256
00:15:06,164 --> 00:15:11,069
We had never spoken one-on-one.

257
00:15:11,269 --> 00:15:15,474
So I assumed we wouldn't get a date.

258
00:15:15,474 --> 00:15:17,876
I was really surprised.

259
00:15:21,813 --> 00:15:24,916
When you become interested in someone,

260
00:15:24,916 --> 00:15:25,984
do you struggle to approach them?

261
00:15:25,984 --> 00:15:27,185
- Yes.
- Right?

262
00:15:27,185 --> 00:15:28,387
I'm like that too.

263
00:15:28,387 --> 00:15:30,522
- I completely freeze up.
- Right.

264
00:15:31,256 --> 00:15:32,958
I actually avoid them.

265
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:33,725
Why?

266
00:15:33,725 --> 00:15:34,526
It's just...

267
00:15:35,394 --> 00:15:37,462
But you're not avoiding me now, so...

268
00:15:37,462 --> 00:15:38,797
(Flustered)

269
00:15:38,797 --> 00:15:40,065
That's not what I meant.

270
00:15:40,065 --> 00:15:43,201
When you like someone,
you should go over...

271
00:15:43,201 --> 00:15:45,737
and start talking to them.

272
00:15:46,405 --> 00:15:48,907
But I find that difficult.

273
00:15:48,907 --> 00:15:51,043
I struggle to make the first move.

274
00:15:52,144 --> 00:15:54,312
Do you avoid them if they approach you?

275
00:15:54,312 --> 00:15:55,814
No, I don't.

276
00:15:56,782 --> 00:15:58,316
Then I understand what you mean.

277
00:15:59,017 --> 00:16:00,719
It seems I struggle...

278
00:16:02,154 --> 00:16:03,388
to make the first move.

279
00:16:05,424 --> 00:16:06,692
We're both like that.

280
00:16:13,298 --> 00:16:16,301
(A date between two shy introverts)

281
00:16:17,336 --> 00:16:18,403
(Sneaks a glance)

282
00:16:20,906 --> 00:16:21,873
Well,

283
00:16:26,311 --> 00:16:29,281
it's still only our first day,

284
00:16:29,915 --> 00:16:31,717
but still,

285
00:16:31,717 --> 00:16:33,685
is there anyone you're interested in?

286
00:16:37,989 --> 00:16:38,857
You.

287
00:16:41,059 --> 00:16:43,495
Seon Ho just answered with his eyes.

288
00:16:43,495 --> 00:16:44,696
(Having so much fun)

289
00:16:44,696 --> 00:16:47,699
His expressive face is so cute.

290
00:16:47,699 --> 00:16:49,368
Seon Ho has quite an intense gaze.

291
00:16:49,368 --> 00:16:50,235
Exactly.

292
00:16:50,235 --> 00:16:51,336
(Heart fluttering)

293
00:16:51,803 --> 00:16:54,039
Since it was the first day,

294
00:16:54,039 --> 00:16:56,608
we all hadn't really talked to each other.

295
00:16:58,176 --> 00:16:59,111
But still,

296
00:17:00,979 --> 00:17:01,847
I must have been interested in you.

297
00:17:01,847 --> 00:17:04,082
Why else would we be on this date now?

298
00:17:05,217 --> 00:17:07,252
What was that?

299
00:17:07,252 --> 00:17:08,587
He delivers when it counts.

300
00:17:08,587 --> 00:17:09,955
Seriously?

301
00:17:09,955 --> 00:17:10,722
Seon Ho.

302
00:17:12,057 --> 00:17:12,958
(Agreed)

303
00:17:12,958 --> 00:17:13,925
"He delivers when it counts."

304
00:17:13,925 --> 00:17:15,994
He can express himself after all.

305
00:17:15,994 --> 00:17:17,929
Look at Seon Ho.

306
00:17:20,799 --> 00:17:22,234
I had no idea.

307
00:17:23,568 --> 00:17:25,837
When we first met,

308
00:17:25,837 --> 00:17:27,673
you seemed like you didn't want to talk.

309
00:17:27,673 --> 00:17:29,608
I was very awkward.

310
00:17:29,608 --> 00:17:31,209
So I thought,

311
00:17:31,209 --> 00:17:34,012
"He has no interest in me at all."

312
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,756
The sky suddenly cleared up.

313
00:17:46,358 --> 00:17:48,060
It's getting hot.

314
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:50,095
(The sky brightens with their mood.)

315
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:56,902
(They head to their next stop.)

316
00:17:57,202 --> 00:17:59,204
We can go in there.

317
00:18:00,839 --> 00:18:02,507
Is it a bookstore?

318
00:18:02,507 --> 00:18:03,275
Yes.

319
00:18:03,275 --> 00:18:04,576
Cool.

320
00:18:06,678 --> 00:18:10,816
(A place he wanted to visit with Ye Ji)

321
00:18:12,317 --> 00:18:15,087
(A small bookstore in an alley)

322
00:18:15,087 --> 00:18:18,056
Are we supposed to write something here?

323
00:18:19,391 --> 00:18:21,259
Let's choose a passage to copy.

324
00:18:21,626 --> 00:18:23,261
Let's each pick one.

325
00:18:25,097 --> 00:18:26,164
(Grinning)

326
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:29,935
As we entered the bookstore,

327
00:18:30,502 --> 00:18:33,972
I thought if she was who I knew,

328
00:18:34,239 --> 00:18:36,541
then coming here...

329
00:18:36,541 --> 00:18:39,478
might help her remember me.

330
00:18:39,478 --> 00:18:40,779
(Startled)

331
00:18:40,779 --> 00:18:41,613
Seriously?

332
00:18:41,613 --> 00:18:44,416
It seemed like Seon Ho wanted something.

333
00:18:44,616 --> 00:18:47,052
But Ye Ji didn't seem...

334
00:18:47,052 --> 00:18:49,888
to notice or sense anything at all.

335
00:18:49,888 --> 00:18:51,189
That makes this even more fun.

336
00:18:52,924 --> 00:18:54,259
(1. Choose a book for your date.)

337
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:55,627
(2. Discuss a sentence that moves you.)

338
00:18:55,627 --> 00:18:56,995
(3. Copy it and give it to someone dear.)

339
00:18:56,995 --> 00:18:58,163
I picked one.

340
00:18:58,163 --> 00:18:59,164
You did?

341
00:19:00,065 --> 00:19:01,867
This is fun. Have you done this before?

342
00:19:02,734 --> 00:19:04,169
(Laughing)

343
00:19:05,237 --> 00:19:07,372
Actually,

344
00:19:08,106 --> 00:19:10,042
while I was bedridden,

345
00:19:12,177 --> 00:19:14,212
I wrote down things that came to mind.

346
00:19:14,212 --> 00:19:18,850
When a passage in a book moved me,

347
00:19:18,850 --> 00:19:20,352
I practiced writing them down.

348
00:19:20,986 --> 00:19:23,121
Then I'd...

349
00:19:23,121 --> 00:19:24,556
post it on my blog from time to time.

350
00:19:25,624 --> 00:19:28,126
You copied passages and posted them?

351
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:31,163
But so much time has passed now.

352
00:19:31,863 --> 00:19:34,433
I don't know if I can write like that now.

353
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,703
But let's give it a try.

354
00:19:38,970 --> 00:19:40,639
I used to copy passages often too.

355
00:19:40,639 --> 00:19:41,773
- You did?
- Yes.

356
00:19:42,174 --> 00:19:43,709
Whenever I found a good passage.

357
00:19:43,709 --> 00:19:45,644
Is there a color you would like?

358
00:19:45,644 --> 00:19:48,146
I'll take purple.

359
00:19:50,015 --> 00:19:51,116
The paper is different too.

360
00:19:52,284 --> 00:19:57,389
(Time moves at a pace all their own.)

361
00:20:05,597 --> 00:20:06,932
"Shining with clarity."

362
00:20:07,666 --> 00:20:09,668
Wait, where should I stamp it?

363
00:20:09,668 --> 00:20:10,969
How about here, like this?

364
00:20:10,969 --> 00:20:12,004
Okay.

365
00:20:12,938 --> 00:20:14,172
(Pressing firmly)

366
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,641
This looks funny.

367
00:20:18,944 --> 00:20:20,312
There isn't enough room.

368
00:20:20,312 --> 00:20:21,213
No.

369
00:20:21,847 --> 00:20:22,848
(The edge of the paper tears.)

370
00:20:22,848 --> 00:20:24,216
It didn't cut cleanly.

371
00:20:24,916 --> 00:20:27,052
I'm basically handing you trash.

372
00:20:27,552 --> 00:20:28,720
The words are what matter.

373
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:29,654
(Awkward)

374
00:20:29,654 --> 00:20:31,323
Shall we exchange them?

375
00:20:31,323 --> 00:20:32,190
I'm sorry.

376
00:20:33,625 --> 00:20:35,060
Let's take a picture of this.

377
00:20:36,662 --> 00:20:37,529
Done.

378
00:20:38,964 --> 00:20:40,532
Why did you choose this for me?

379
00:20:40,532 --> 00:20:41,533
Does it have a special meaning?

380
00:20:41,533 --> 00:20:43,502
It really spoke to me.

381
00:20:43,502 --> 00:20:45,037
(The lines Ye Ji gave Seon Ho)

382
00:20:47,039 --> 00:20:50,409
(The lines Seon Ho gave Ye Ji)

383
00:20:58,283 --> 00:21:03,255
(They slowly read each other's hearts.)

384
00:21:03,689 --> 00:21:05,791
I'll keep this safe.

385
00:21:05,791 --> 00:21:08,360
(Laughing)

386
00:21:09,027 --> 00:21:10,462
I'll make sure it doesn't tear more.

387
00:21:10,462 --> 00:21:11,596
How should I keep this?

388
00:21:11,596 --> 00:21:13,265
I'll put mine in here like this.

389
00:21:19,705 --> 00:21:22,274
Can I ask you something?

390
00:21:22,274 --> 00:21:23,475
You have blogged for a long time, right?

391
00:21:23,475 --> 00:21:24,476
Yes.

392
00:21:24,476 --> 00:21:25,243
So...

393
00:21:26,745 --> 00:21:29,981
do any of your blog followers stand out?

394
00:21:34,419 --> 00:21:35,354
Blog?

395
00:21:37,823 --> 00:21:38,757
A connection?

396
00:21:38,757 --> 00:21:40,258
His expression is intriguing.

397
00:21:43,095 --> 00:21:44,963
When I was really struggling,

398
00:21:44,963 --> 00:21:48,066
someone visited my blog daily to pray.

399
00:21:48,834 --> 00:21:49,601
I see.

400
00:21:49,601 --> 00:21:51,136
That always amazed me.

401
00:21:51,136 --> 00:21:52,938
That person wasn't family.

402
00:21:52,938 --> 00:21:56,675
In a way, we had no connection at all.

403
00:21:56,675 --> 00:22:00,512
Yet they remembered me and prayed daily.

404
00:22:00,512 --> 00:22:04,483
That person is the one I remember most.

405
00:22:04,483 --> 00:22:08,720
And some people always comment first.

406
00:22:09,621 --> 00:22:12,190
Some people I met in 2018...

407
00:22:12,190 --> 00:22:15,560
still leave comments to this day.

408
00:22:16,595 --> 00:22:18,997
They say they enjoy my posts,

409
00:22:18,997 --> 00:22:20,666
and now,

410
00:22:20,666 --> 00:22:22,534
they no longer want
my battle-against-illness diary.

411
00:22:22,534 --> 00:22:25,037
They want to read about my daily life.

412
00:22:25,771 --> 00:22:28,840
My blog is still titled
"Battle-Against-Illness Diary."

413
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:32,511
The title and content don't quite match.

414
00:22:32,511 --> 00:22:35,113
But that makes me very happy.

415
00:22:35,113 --> 00:22:39,051
I finally got to see this day.

416
00:22:40,452 --> 00:22:43,188
I had desperately hoped for the day...

417
00:22:43,188 --> 00:22:46,024
when I could share my everyday life.

418
00:22:46,425 --> 00:22:47,326
So...

419
00:22:52,531 --> 00:22:53,632
What is it?

420
00:22:53,632 --> 00:22:55,967
- Hurry up.
- Say it.

421
00:22:55,967 --> 00:22:57,969
Look at that smile.

422
00:22:57,969 --> 00:23:00,205
- Seon Ho is dying to say it.
- Exactly.

423
00:23:00,205 --> 00:23:02,641
He's itching to get it out.

424
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:05,267
Well...

425
00:23:09,972 --> 00:23:10,839
Actually,

426
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:14,376
I think you're the person I know.

427
00:23:15,477 --> 00:23:17,212
What? What do you mean?

428
00:23:26,522 --> 00:23:28,857
(Hesitating)

429
00:23:30,025 --> 00:23:32,661
I think you and I are blog friends.

430
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:34,563
- What? Seriously?
- Yes.

431
00:23:37,232 --> 00:23:39,568
I've even seen your recent posts.

432
00:23:42,237 --> 00:23:43,539
Goodness.

433
00:23:43,539 --> 00:23:44,439
What?

434
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:46,842
I've got chills.

435
00:23:49,278 --> 00:23:51,013
Seriously? Wait.

436
00:23:51,013 --> 00:23:52,014
Seriously?

437
00:23:53,148 --> 00:23:54,349
Goodness.

438
00:23:54,349 --> 00:23:56,585
That must be why he struggled to talk.

439
00:23:56,585 --> 00:23:58,554
It must be.

440
00:23:58,554 --> 00:23:59,588
I've got chills.

441
00:24:01,256 --> 00:24:04,793
That's why I had my suspicions yesterday.

442
00:24:04,793 --> 00:24:05,527
Seriously?

443
00:24:06,295 --> 00:24:07,763
Wait, that's...

444
00:24:08,730 --> 00:24:10,432
(Laughing)

445
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:19,842
Your name suddenly sounded familiar.

446
00:24:21,443 --> 00:24:23,679
When Ye Ji first entered the house,

447
00:24:25,614 --> 00:24:30,285
she looked like the person from the blog.

448
00:24:32,054 --> 00:24:33,755
I wasn't sure at first.

449
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:35,824
I'll read it.

450
00:24:37,926 --> 00:24:43,098
But yesterday, when she read her diary,

451
00:24:43,098 --> 00:24:44,333
I became almost certain.

452
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,436
My body was covered in tubes and wires.

453
00:24:48,136 --> 00:24:49,838
When my grandmother reached my room,

454
00:24:49,838 --> 00:24:51,940
she saw me and burst into tears.

455
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:53,775
I told her, "Do not cry."

456
00:24:57,446 --> 00:25:00,716
You know how certain lines stick with you?

457
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:02,885
I knew I'd heard it before.

458
00:25:08,190 --> 00:25:09,758
Would you like some water?

459
00:25:13,762 --> 00:25:19,201
(Seon Ho quietly took care of Ye Ji.)

460
00:25:22,871 --> 00:25:25,440
When I first began treatment,

461
00:25:26,842 --> 00:25:28,984
I started a blog.

462
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:35,484
(Seon Ho's first post from 2020,
when his treatment began)

463
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:39,888
I remember Ye Ji commenting first.

464
00:25:39,888 --> 00:25:42,858
She left a comment on my post.

465
00:25:42,858 --> 00:25:44,526
It was a message cheering me on.

466
00:25:44,927 --> 00:25:48,130
(You were diagnosed during service.
That breaks my heart.)

467
00:25:48,130 --> 00:25:51,266
(I'll cheer for your full recovery.
We can beat this together.)

468
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:55,137
(Thank you for reading my posts
and supporting me.)

469
00:25:55,137 --> 00:25:58,607
(I'll cheer for you too.
We can beat this.)

470
00:25:59,408 --> 00:26:01,143
(Stunned)

471
00:26:01,443 --> 00:26:03,245
Goodness.

472
00:26:03,245 --> 00:26:04,346
That's incredible.

473
00:26:04,346 --> 00:26:05,280
How is that possible?

474
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:07,916
This is unbelievable.

475
00:26:07,916 --> 00:26:09,861
No movie could top this story.

476
00:26:09,862 --> 00:26:10,586
Seriously.

477
00:26:10,886 --> 00:26:13,121
He was sick himself,

478
00:26:13,121 --> 00:26:16,358
but he still read her blog and commented.

479
00:26:16,358 --> 00:26:18,861
Her posts gave him strength and hope.

480
00:26:19,628 --> 00:26:21,563
And now he was meeting her in person.

481
00:26:21,563 --> 00:26:22,564
She was even the first one to come in.

482
00:26:22,564 --> 00:26:23,632
Goodness.

483
00:26:23,632 --> 00:26:25,133
This has to be fate.

484
00:26:25,133 --> 00:26:26,568
It's fate.

485
00:26:26,802 --> 00:26:28,437
This is seriously incredible.

486
00:26:30,572 --> 00:26:32,608
(A connection only Seon Ho remembered)

487
00:26:32,608 --> 00:26:33,909
I really want to find those comments.

488
00:26:40,582 --> 00:26:44,052
He said we exchanged comments
six years ago.

489
00:26:44,052 --> 00:26:46,321
I was stunned.

490
00:26:46,321 --> 00:26:49,291
I wondered what we had talked about.

491
00:26:49,291 --> 00:26:51,727
As we discussed it,

492
00:26:51,727 --> 00:26:54,229
I felt myself open up to him.

493
00:26:54,229 --> 00:26:56,565
It was amazing that six years ago,

494
00:26:56,565 --> 00:27:00,802
we already knew each other in some way.

495
00:27:01,270 --> 00:27:04,640
I realized things like this really happen.

496
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:06,775
That was how I felt.

497
00:27:06,776 --> 00:27:07,743
(They come to face each other
after six years)

498
00:27:07,743 --> 00:27:10,179
Goodness, six years ago.

499
00:27:10,179 --> 00:27:11,914
What is this? Was it set up?

500
00:27:11,914 --> 00:27:13,749
We imagined so many possibilities.

501
00:27:13,749 --> 00:27:14,950
This is beyond anything we imagined.

502
00:27:14,950 --> 00:27:16,018
It really is.

503
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:18,387
You didn't cast them knowing, did you?

504
00:27:19,354 --> 00:27:22,357
Did you find out before casting them?

505
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:23,659
They had no idea.

506
00:27:23,659 --> 00:27:25,060
You really knew nothing?

507
00:27:25,961 --> 00:27:26,829
Unbelievable.

508
00:27:26,829 --> 00:27:27,796
Incredible.

509
00:27:27,796 --> 00:27:29,731
It wasn't just any comment.
It was private.

510
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:30,866
(Surprised)

511
00:27:31,633 --> 00:27:33,535
You saw the padlock on it earlier, right?

512
00:27:37,139 --> 00:27:39,575
(Ye Ji)

513
00:27:39,575 --> 00:27:42,678
(Kim Seon Ho, blog owner)

514
00:27:43,011 --> 00:27:46,715
So I already knew what you did...

515
00:27:46,715 --> 00:27:47,983
and roughly how old you were.

516
00:27:47,983 --> 00:27:49,918
Wait, isn't that cheating?

517
00:27:50,853 --> 00:27:54,189
I chose you for this date...

518
00:27:55,023 --> 00:27:56,692
partly to see
if you were the person I knew.

519
00:27:57,159 --> 00:28:00,195
I wanted to know for sure.

520
00:28:00,696 --> 00:28:02,965
The person I knew worked incredibly hard.

521
00:28:04,166 --> 00:28:07,736
I saw her attend a university in Seoul.

522
00:28:09,872 --> 00:28:11,874
I saw her graduate.

523
00:28:11,874 --> 00:28:13,475
I even saw her graduation photos.

524
00:28:14,243 --> 00:28:15,811
This is unbelievable.

525
00:28:15,811 --> 00:28:17,412
How could this...

526
00:28:20,616 --> 00:28:23,051
I feel completely blindsided.

527
00:28:27,656 --> 00:28:28,957
(Sneaks a glance)

528
00:28:29,591 --> 00:28:31,393
But this is fun.

529
00:28:33,629 --> 00:28:36,298
I honestly don't know how to react.

530
00:28:38,066 --> 00:28:39,701
I think my brain just froze.

531
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:50,612
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

532
00:28:50,612 --> 00:28:53,282
(Kim Seon Ho and Jung Ye Ji,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

533
00:28:53,916 --> 00:28:57,219
(Their time runs out before they know it.)

534
00:28:57,953 --> 00:28:59,221
No.

535
00:28:59,221 --> 00:29:00,889
(Disappointed)

536
00:29:00,889 --> 00:29:02,324
No.

537
00:29:02,324 --> 00:29:04,526
They only learned from this message...

538
00:29:04,526 --> 00:29:06,795
that their date would last...

539
00:29:06,795 --> 00:29:08,764
as long as the time they gave each other.

540
00:29:08,764 --> 00:29:11,233
They found out only just now.

541
00:29:11,233 --> 00:29:12,534
The message said they used 100 minutes.

542
00:29:12,534 --> 00:29:14,236
Amazing.

543
00:29:14,236 --> 00:29:18,273
Now they know how much each person gave.

544
00:29:18,273 --> 00:29:20,609
How they interpret that...

545
00:29:20,609 --> 00:29:21,910
will surely vary.

546
00:29:21,910 --> 00:29:23,178
I'm curious.

547
00:29:26,849 --> 00:29:30,185
What are you doing after this date?

548
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:31,253
After this?

549
00:29:32,054 --> 00:29:34,490
I'm not sure what to do.

550
00:29:34,490 --> 00:29:36,158
I may just cook something to eat.

551
00:29:36,859 --> 00:29:38,160
- You must be hungry.
- Yes.

552
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,061
Me too.

553
00:29:45,467 --> 00:29:47,836
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

554
00:29:47,836 --> 00:29:49,605
(Jung Ye Ji and Kim Seon Ho,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

555
00:29:49,605 --> 00:29:51,106
Did you receive a message?

556
00:29:51,106 --> 00:29:51,807
Yes.

557
00:29:52,708 --> 00:29:57,279
(Ye Ji, 50 minutes / Seon Ho, 50 minutes)

558
00:29:58,747 --> 00:30:02,918
"Your 100-minute date is over."

559
00:30:02,918 --> 00:30:05,120
That message came in,

560
00:30:05,387 --> 00:30:08,190
and I was completely immersed.

561
00:30:08,190 --> 00:30:11,426
I couldn't believe this story was real.

562
00:30:11,426 --> 00:30:14,329
Just as I was reeling from that,

563
00:30:14,329 --> 00:30:18,000
I learned he had given
someone else 50 minutes.

564
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:19,201
I wondered who it was.

565
00:30:20,335 --> 00:30:22,204
I was very curious.

566
00:30:23,005 --> 00:30:25,073
I gave Ye Ji 50 minutes.

567
00:30:25,073 --> 00:30:26,942
She had given me 50 minutes too.

568
00:30:27,242 --> 00:30:30,078
Fifty out of her 100 minutes...

569
00:30:30,913 --> 00:30:33,248
felt like a significant amount.

570
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:38,453
I was glad she viewed me positively.

571
00:30:38,453 --> 00:30:40,022
That made me happy.

572
00:30:40,756 --> 00:30:42,324
- There it is.
- See?

573
00:30:42,324 --> 00:30:44,893
That's how he chose to look at it.

574
00:30:44,893 --> 00:30:47,396
That's why choosing wisely matters.

575
00:30:47,396 --> 00:30:48,430
It's like looking at a glass...

576
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:50,465
and seeing it as half full...

577
00:30:50,465 --> 00:30:51,767
or half empty.

578
00:30:51,767 --> 00:30:53,268
Fifty minutes can be taken differently.

579
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:54,236
It really does.

580
00:30:56,171 --> 00:31:01,443
(With 6 years apart and different takes
on 50 minutes, their first date ends.)

581
00:31:01,877 --> 00:31:05,214
(Cheonggyecheon Stream)

582
00:31:07,149 --> 00:31:10,352
(Do Gon waits alone.)

583
00:31:13,655 --> 00:31:14,890
As I waited,

584
00:31:14,890 --> 00:31:17,459
since I knew Ro Bin would come...

585
00:31:17,459 --> 00:31:21,730
because I'd given her all 100 minutes,
I was excited.

586
00:31:21,730 --> 00:31:24,333
I wondered where she would appear,

587
00:31:24,333 --> 00:31:25,701
how the date would go, how I'd feel,

588
00:31:25,701 --> 00:31:27,636
and what the whole moment would be like.

589
00:31:33,675 --> 00:31:34,943
(Spotted)

590
00:31:35,911 --> 00:31:37,212
(Shy)

591
00:31:37,779 --> 00:31:40,616
Do Gon showed up.

592
00:31:40,616 --> 00:31:43,852
I was shocked. I never expected him.

593
00:31:43,852 --> 00:31:48,123
He doesn't react strongly,

594
00:31:48,457 --> 00:31:51,126
so I didn't think he would come.

595
00:31:53,495 --> 00:31:54,596
Hello.

596
00:31:55,063 --> 00:31:57,065
I had no idea. I didn't expect you.

597
00:31:57,065 --> 00:31:58,267
- Really?
- Yes.

598
00:31:59,468 --> 00:32:02,404
I heard you planned our date.

599
00:32:02,404 --> 00:32:03,906
First of all,

600
00:32:03,906 --> 00:32:05,807
do you like vintage clothing stores?

601
00:32:05,807 --> 00:32:08,710
Absolutely. I love vintage shops.

602
00:32:08,710 --> 00:32:10,245
- Really?
- I love them.

603
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:12,414
Are we going to a vintage shop?

604
00:32:12,414 --> 00:32:13,982
Are we going to shop for clothes?

605
00:32:13,982 --> 00:32:16,018
We can browse clothes and other things.

606
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:17,152
Great.

607
00:32:18,020 --> 00:32:19,087
That sounds fun.

608
00:32:21,056 --> 00:32:22,324
It sounds like so much fun.

609
00:32:23,225 --> 00:32:24,193
On your way here...

610
00:32:25,961 --> 00:32:26,929
Yes?

611
00:32:26,929 --> 00:32:28,564
who did you expect?

612
00:32:28,564 --> 00:32:31,934
I really didn't expect you, Do Gon.

613
00:32:31,934 --> 00:32:33,202
- Really?
- Yes.

614
00:32:34,436 --> 00:32:37,439
Though we only talked briefly,

615
00:32:37,439 --> 00:32:40,209
we seemed to have much in common.

616
00:32:40,209 --> 00:32:41,376
Really?

617
00:32:41,944 --> 00:32:44,112
So I wanted to know more.

618
00:32:44,112 --> 00:32:45,714
I wanted to talk to you.

619
00:32:47,950 --> 00:32:51,086
I see. You didn't show it at all.

620
00:32:51,086 --> 00:32:52,221
I had no idea.

621
00:32:54,022 --> 00:32:56,191
I'm showing it little by little.

622
00:32:58,293 --> 00:33:00,229
(Dongmyo)

623
00:33:00,229 --> 00:33:01,563
There are so many people.

624
00:33:02,531 --> 00:33:05,601
It's busier because it's the weekend.

625
00:33:06,468 --> 00:33:08,637
We had dinner pretty early yesterday,

626
00:33:08,637 --> 00:33:10,172
so I was starving before bed.

627
00:33:11,006 --> 00:33:13,575
But I was tired,
so I went to sleep anyway.

628
00:33:13,575 --> 00:33:15,644
But your stomach kept growling.

629
00:33:20,382 --> 00:33:21,483
This way.

630
00:33:21,483 --> 00:33:22,985
This way? Cool.

631
00:33:22,985 --> 00:33:24,319
(They soon reach a vintage shop.)

632
00:33:25,254 --> 00:33:26,522
Hello.

633
00:33:27,289 --> 00:33:28,457
Hello.

634
00:33:30,826 --> 00:33:31,994
Take your time looking around.

635
00:33:32,594 --> 00:33:34,363
Then we can...

636
00:33:34,363 --> 00:33:36,064
Pick something for each other?

637
00:33:36,064 --> 00:33:36,932
Shall we give it a try?

638
00:33:36,932 --> 00:33:39,635
I don't know much about men's clothes.

639
00:33:40,169 --> 00:33:43,305
(They choose clothes for each other.)

640
00:33:45,874 --> 00:33:47,776
It looks a little small, right?

641
00:33:47,776 --> 00:33:48,577
Yes.

642
00:33:48,577 --> 00:33:50,078
(Studying it closely)

643
00:33:50,746 --> 00:33:51,780
It looks a little small.

644
00:33:52,314 --> 00:33:53,415
Or you can try it.

645
00:33:53,682 --> 00:33:55,050
Me?

646
00:33:55,050 --> 00:33:55,884
Something oversized.

647
00:33:55,884 --> 00:33:57,886
I like oversized clothes.

648
00:33:57,886 --> 00:33:58,787
What do you think?

649
00:33:58,787 --> 00:34:00,055
It may be too big.

650
00:34:00,055 --> 00:34:01,190
Do you think so?

651
00:34:01,924 --> 00:34:02,991
Let me look in the mirror.

652
00:34:04,259 --> 00:34:06,461
- It's too big.
- Right? It's huge.

653
00:34:06,962 --> 00:34:08,330
I'd never done that before.

654
00:34:08,330 --> 00:34:10,199
I was honestly very shy.

655
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:12,634
I didn't know what to choose for him.

656
00:34:12,634 --> 00:34:15,604
What if he disliked what I picked?

657
00:34:16,305 --> 00:34:17,139
She's adorable.

658
00:34:17,139 --> 00:34:18,173
That's cute.

659
00:34:18,173 --> 00:34:20,075
Everything here is a first for her.

660
00:34:20,075 --> 00:34:21,476
Everything is new to her.

661
00:34:21,476 --> 00:34:23,011
It's her first date.

662
00:34:23,245 --> 00:34:24,847
It's her first time choosing his clothes.

663
00:34:24,847 --> 00:34:26,748
"I like this oversized vest."

664
00:34:26,748 --> 00:34:28,884
She doesn't know what to say.

665
00:34:28,884 --> 00:34:30,185
(For lifelong single Ro Bin, all is new.)

666
00:34:31,286 --> 00:34:32,855
This is so pretty.

667
00:34:32,855 --> 00:34:33,789
Right?

668
00:34:34,122 --> 00:34:35,657
(Ro Bin chooses Do Gon's outfit.)

669
00:34:35,657 --> 00:34:37,626
It would look nice with navy shorts.

670
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:39,995
This is bright orange.

671
00:34:40,863 --> 00:34:42,931
- It looks nice.
- What do you think?

672
00:34:42,931 --> 00:34:43,999
It looks good.

673
00:34:47,135 --> 00:34:48,036
Try it on.

674
00:34:49,571 --> 00:34:52,007
(They try on
what they chose for each other.)

675
00:34:53,509 --> 00:34:55,310
Ro Bin, I'll change quickly too.

676
00:34:55,310 --> 00:34:56,111
All right.

677
00:34:57,913 --> 00:35:01,350
(Do Gon wears the outfit Ro Bin chose.)

678
00:35:06,255 --> 00:35:07,456
(Satisfied)

679
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:12,961
(Click)

680
00:35:15,998 --> 00:35:17,232
I put it on.

681
00:35:17,232 --> 00:35:19,868
(He can't take his eyes off Ro Bin.)

682
00:35:20,936 --> 00:35:24,239
It looks nice.
I usually roll up my sleeves.

683
00:35:24,239 --> 00:35:26,175
- Like this.
- The shoulders...

684
00:35:26,175 --> 00:35:28,577
It's a bit large, but it may be fine.

685
00:35:30,712 --> 00:35:33,615
- Do not touch her.
- What was that?

686
00:35:33,615 --> 00:35:34,750
Do Gon.

687
00:35:34,750 --> 00:35:36,051
(Bursts out laughing)

688
00:35:36,818 --> 00:35:38,620
(Completely immersed)

689
00:35:38,954 --> 00:35:40,823
- That's cute.
- Look at them.

690
00:35:41,924 --> 00:35:42,858
This is so...

691
00:35:42,858 --> 00:35:44,059
That would make my heart flutter.

692
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:45,861
That's cute.

693
00:35:46,728 --> 00:35:48,330
Should I roll these up or leave them down?

694
00:35:48,330 --> 00:35:50,032
- Rolled up is much better.
- Is it?

695
00:35:50,032 --> 00:35:51,600
But don't roll them too far.

696
00:35:53,335 --> 00:35:55,103
(He rolls Ro Bin's sleeves for her.)

697
00:35:55,103 --> 00:35:55,871
About that much?

698
00:35:56,839 --> 00:35:58,173
(Gently)

699
00:35:58,674 --> 00:36:00,008
Tell me if it's uncomfortable.

700
00:36:00,008 --> 00:36:01,310
Not at all.

701
00:36:01,944 --> 00:36:05,581
He helped me into the shirt
and rolled my sleeves.

702
00:36:05,914 --> 00:36:10,519
I never knew that having a man...

703
00:36:10,519 --> 00:36:12,888
roll up my sleeves would make...

704
00:36:12,888 --> 00:36:14,456
my heart flutter so much.

705
00:36:14,756 --> 00:36:16,124
The sleeves...

706
00:36:16,124 --> 00:36:17,292
Yeah.

707
00:36:18,694 --> 00:36:19,695
This is embarrassing.

708
00:36:22,798 --> 00:36:23,832
About this much?

709
00:36:25,701 --> 00:36:26,668
Nice.

710
00:36:26,935 --> 00:36:28,670
(Perfect)

711
00:36:28,670 --> 00:36:30,038
(Thumbs up)

712
00:36:30,038 --> 00:36:31,240
- Like that.
- Like this?

713
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:32,708
- Yes.
- Great.

714
00:36:32,708 --> 00:36:35,777
That outfit really brightens your face.

715
00:36:35,777 --> 00:36:38,213
- Right?
- It suits you very well.

716
00:36:38,213 --> 00:36:39,281
(Their first shopping trip is a success.)

717
00:36:40,115 --> 00:36:41,717
- All right, this one.
- All right.

718
00:36:41,950 --> 00:36:44,820
I don't own many bright-colored clothes.

719
00:36:44,820 --> 00:36:46,722
So I wanted to buy something bright,

720
00:36:47,523 --> 00:36:49,558
and she happened
to pick something perfect.

721
00:36:50,459 --> 00:36:51,460
I really like it.

722
00:36:53,362 --> 00:36:54,196
This...

723
00:36:55,330 --> 00:36:56,632
- I...
- Yes?

724
00:36:59,902 --> 00:37:02,004
brought a film camera.

725
00:37:02,004 --> 00:37:03,205
Really?

726
00:37:03,205 --> 00:37:05,007
Great.

727
00:37:05,007 --> 00:37:06,408
Let's take one with it.

728
00:37:06,408 --> 00:37:07,976
I'd love that.

729
00:37:09,845 --> 00:37:11,713
Shall we take it here,
since we bought them here?

730
00:37:11,713 --> 00:37:12,648
Sure.

731
00:37:13,348 --> 00:37:14,616
Please take a photo of me.

732
00:37:14,616 --> 00:37:17,386
(They capture this moment on film.)

733
00:37:17,653 --> 00:37:19,655
(Coming through)

734
00:37:19,822 --> 00:37:21,256
(Laughing)

735
00:37:23,058 --> 00:37:25,694
One, two, three.

736
00:37:25,694 --> 00:37:26,562
(Peace sign)

737
00:37:26,562 --> 00:37:27,796
Got it.

738
00:37:27,796 --> 00:37:29,932
I'll take one for you with this.

739
00:37:30,132 --> 00:37:31,433
Please take mine too.

740
00:37:31,433 --> 00:37:32,267
Let's take a picture.

741
00:37:33,135 --> 00:37:36,238
One, two, three.

742
00:37:36,238 --> 00:37:37,139
(Peace sign)

743
00:37:37,606 --> 00:37:41,076
(Ro Bin, photographed by Do Gon)

744
00:37:41,076 --> 00:37:44,746
(Do Gon, photographed by Ro Bin)

745
00:37:44,746 --> 00:37:45,681
Let's take a selfie.

746
00:37:45,681 --> 00:37:46,715
A selfie?

747
00:37:46,715 --> 00:37:49,818
(Their first photo together)

748
00:37:50,052 --> 00:37:51,453
So cute.

749
00:37:51,453 --> 00:37:52,688
(Their hearts race.)

750
00:37:52,688 --> 00:37:54,223
- That makes my heart flutter.
- It does.

751
00:37:54,223 --> 00:37:55,657
- My heart is racing.
- I love this.

752
00:37:55,657 --> 00:37:57,726
The film camera was a nice touch.

753
00:37:57,726 --> 00:37:58,927
Bringing it was a great call.

754
00:37:59,428 --> 00:38:01,363
Do Gon seems like a great guy.

755
00:38:01,363 --> 00:38:02,431
He really is.

756
00:38:02,431 --> 00:38:03,198
He has great taste, right?

757
00:38:03,198 --> 00:38:04,733
His taste is amazing.

758
00:38:04,733 --> 00:38:05,801
(Bursts out laughing)

759
00:38:05,801 --> 00:38:08,337
He says it in that gentle Do Gon way,

760
00:38:08,337 --> 00:38:09,605
so it doesn't feel overwhelming.

761
00:38:11,673 --> 00:38:14,142
- Look at this.
- It looks tiny.

762
00:38:14,142 --> 00:38:16,945
This is brand-new.

763
00:38:16,945 --> 00:38:19,214
This one is a gift for you, Ro Bin.

764
00:38:19,214 --> 00:38:20,582
- Seriously?
- Yes.

765
00:38:20,582 --> 00:38:21,817
I love it. I should put it away.

766
00:38:21,817 --> 00:38:23,285
I have the same one.

767
00:38:23,285 --> 00:38:24,520
I brought an extra.

768
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:25,587
So while we're here,

769
00:38:26,388 --> 00:38:29,591
use it to photograph whatever you like.

770
00:38:30,726 --> 00:38:31,693
With this?

771
00:38:31,693 --> 00:38:33,462
You mean anything I want?

772
00:38:33,462 --> 00:38:34,530
Great.

773
00:38:34,530 --> 00:38:36,231
I love it.

774
00:38:36,465 --> 00:38:38,467
I'd planned to bring a film camera too.

775
00:38:38,467 --> 00:38:40,035
(They grow closer as time passes.)

776
00:38:40,035 --> 00:38:41,403
This is so meaningful.

777
00:38:43,405 --> 00:38:47,376
When I visit Dongmyo,
I stop by here sometimes.

778
00:38:48,510 --> 00:38:49,912
(They arrive at Do Gon's regular spot.)

779
00:38:49,912 --> 00:38:51,013
Hello.

780
00:38:51,013 --> 00:38:52,281
Hello.

781
00:38:54,483 --> 00:38:55,751
We can sit there.

782
00:38:55,751 --> 00:38:56,885
Here.

783
00:38:58,086 --> 00:39:02,424
(Their first meal alone together)

784
00:39:03,959 --> 00:39:05,727
(Looking around)

785
00:39:06,895 --> 00:39:07,996
Fish roe and milt noodle soup?

786
00:39:07,996 --> 00:39:09,364
Fish roe and milt noodle soup.

787
00:39:09,598 --> 00:39:11,166
The spicy one.

788
00:39:11,667 --> 00:39:15,137
Clam noodle soup. That one is not spicy.

789
00:39:15,137 --> 00:39:16,572
A clean, mild flavor?

790
00:39:16,572 --> 00:39:18,073
- One of each?
- That sounds good.

791
00:39:18,907 --> 00:39:21,510
One roe and milt and one clam, please.

792
00:39:22,711 --> 00:39:25,681
(He quickly orders like a regular.)

793
00:39:26,615 --> 00:39:29,184
Did you change much...

794
00:39:29,184 --> 00:39:31,687
after going through treatment?

795
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:33,822
For me,

796
00:39:33,822 --> 00:39:35,090
I changed a great deal.

797
00:39:35,090 --> 00:39:35,958
What changed the most?

798
00:39:35,958 --> 00:39:37,059
Before treatment,

799
00:39:37,693 --> 00:39:40,229
I was very pessimistic.

800
00:39:40,229 --> 00:39:41,763
I was completely negative.

801
00:39:41,763 --> 00:39:42,865
In general?

802
00:39:43,398 --> 00:39:44,366
Can you give me an example?

803
00:39:45,501 --> 00:39:46,902
I hated the sunrise.

804
00:39:47,703 --> 00:39:50,439
I'd wake up and dread another sunrise.

805
00:39:51,406 --> 00:39:55,210
I wished night would come
and the day would just end.

806
00:39:55,210 --> 00:39:57,779
That was my general outlook on life.

807
00:39:57,779 --> 00:39:58,847
But...

808
00:39:58,847 --> 00:40:00,716
I'm completely different now.

809
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:02,851
The exact opposite?

810
00:40:02,851 --> 00:40:04,786
- The exact opposite.
- You like sunlight?

811
00:40:04,786 --> 00:40:08,056
Even when things don't go my way,

812
00:40:08,056 --> 00:40:09,024
I tell myself it's all right.

813
00:40:09,892 --> 00:40:12,528
I tell myself, "I can do this."
That's how I think now.

814
00:40:12,928 --> 00:40:14,963
After going through an illness,

815
00:40:14,963 --> 00:40:17,933
do you not naturally grow grateful
for each day?

816
00:40:17,933 --> 00:40:21,336
You appreciate even the smallest things.

817
00:40:21,336 --> 00:40:23,005
Right. That was the biggest change for me.

818
00:40:24,072 --> 00:40:25,874
Exactly. Me too.

819
00:40:29,745 --> 00:40:31,213
Here they are.

820
00:40:31,213 --> 00:40:32,447
Where should I place this dish?

821
00:40:32,447 --> 00:40:33,916
In the middle, please.

822
00:40:36,451 --> 00:40:37,886
Thank you.

823
00:40:37,886 --> 00:40:39,655
I haven't had noodle soup in ages.

824
00:40:39,655 --> 00:40:41,156
It's been a while for me too.

825
00:40:42,057 --> 00:40:43,992
This may be spicy,

826
00:40:43,992 --> 00:40:45,761
- so let's try this one first.
- This one?

827
00:40:46,261 --> 00:40:48,630
I prefer lightly seasoned food.

828
00:40:48,630 --> 00:40:50,866
Right, you said you avoid salty food.

829
00:40:51,133 --> 00:40:52,668
Of course, this isn't exactly...

830
00:40:52,668 --> 00:40:54,369
what we would call lightly seasoned.

831
00:40:55,504 --> 00:40:57,673
Thank you.

832
00:40:57,673 --> 00:40:59,608
(Do Gon serves Ro Bin first.)

833
00:41:00,876 --> 00:41:01,877
Thank you for the meal.

834
00:41:01,877 --> 00:41:03,011
Enjoy.

835
00:41:03,946 --> 00:41:05,147
(Eating)

836
00:41:09,785 --> 00:41:10,719
Good.

837
00:41:13,622 --> 00:41:14,756
On your way here today,

838
00:41:15,757 --> 00:41:17,459
who did you think would be waiting?

839
00:41:18,160 --> 00:41:21,563
I honestly had no idea.

840
00:41:21,563 --> 00:41:23,866
I couldn't tell who my date would be.

841
00:41:23,866 --> 00:41:25,367
- You had no guess?
- No.

842
00:41:25,767 --> 00:41:28,103
I really had no clue.

843
00:41:28,103 --> 00:41:30,072
(Ro Bin didn't notice Do Gon's interest.)

844
00:41:31,273 --> 00:41:33,475
Actually, when you first...

845
00:41:33,475 --> 00:41:35,277
entered the house,

846
00:41:35,277 --> 00:41:36,712
I felt...

847
00:41:38,046 --> 00:41:39,882
You know, the energy people give off...

848
00:41:39,882 --> 00:41:43,218
and their general nature, right?

849
00:41:43,519 --> 00:41:45,988
I thought yours might be similar to mine.

850
00:41:45,988 --> 00:41:46,855
Really?

851
00:41:48,357 --> 00:41:49,892
I don't know yet.

852
00:41:49,892 --> 00:41:51,260
We could be completely different.

853
00:41:51,260 --> 00:41:53,162
You felt that from my first impression?

854
00:41:53,462 --> 00:41:57,132
I thought we might share something.

855
00:41:57,132 --> 00:41:58,767
You got that feeling?

856
00:41:58,767 --> 00:42:00,002
I see.

857
00:42:04,973 --> 00:42:07,176
Even our trip to the vintage shop...

858
00:42:07,176 --> 00:42:08,810
was something I wanted to do on a date.

859
00:42:08,810 --> 00:42:11,713
I wanted to choose my date's outfit,

860
00:42:11,713 --> 00:42:14,082
then spend the day together...

861
00:42:14,449 --> 00:42:17,252
in outfits we picked for each other...

862
00:42:17,252 --> 00:42:19,555
and take photos everywhere we went.

863
00:42:19,555 --> 00:42:20,956
I see.

864
00:42:20,956 --> 00:42:22,457
You've never done this before?

865
00:42:22,791 --> 00:42:24,259
Never.

866
00:42:24,259 --> 00:42:26,195
So I wanted to try it.

867
00:42:26,195 --> 00:42:28,297
Today was the perfect opportunity.

868
00:42:28,297 --> 00:42:30,599
I really had so much fun.

869
00:42:30,599 --> 00:42:32,267
Do not take it off as soon as we get back.

870
00:42:33,402 --> 00:42:34,403
I won't.

871
00:42:35,671 --> 00:42:38,707
(They make a promise of their own.)

872
00:42:42,277 --> 00:42:44,413
- Are you finished?
- Yes, I'm so full.

873
00:42:45,414 --> 00:42:47,282
That was delicious. I really enjoyed it.

874
00:42:49,151 --> 00:42:53,088
(Their satisfying meal comes to an end.)

875
00:42:59,862 --> 00:43:04,500
(They leave the restaurant.)

876
00:43:10,105 --> 00:43:12,541
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

877
00:43:12,541 --> 00:43:18,480
(Han Do Gon and Seo Ro Bin,
your 110-minute date has ended.)

878
00:43:18,714 --> 00:43:22,417
(Do Gon checks the message first.)

879
00:43:22,417 --> 00:43:23,986
Bye.

880
00:43:24,486 --> 00:43:25,988
Bye.

881
00:43:27,156 --> 00:43:28,056
I see.

882
00:43:33,862 --> 00:43:37,032
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

883
00:43:37,032 --> 00:43:41,170
(Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon,
your 110-minute date has ended.)

884
00:43:42,671 --> 00:43:44,273
(Do Gon, 100 minutes)

885
00:43:44,273 --> 00:43:45,841
(Ro Bin, 10 minutes)

886
00:43:45,841 --> 00:43:46,742
I had no idea...

887
00:43:47,376 --> 00:43:50,179
the numbers would be shown like that.

888
00:43:50,179 --> 00:43:53,582
I thought it would only say,
"Your date has ended."

889
00:43:53,582 --> 00:43:56,218
I never expected the exact numbers.

890
00:43:56,485 --> 00:43:58,086
So I just...

891
00:43:59,288 --> 00:44:00,756
We would have to...

892
00:44:00,756 --> 00:44:04,059
talk about how much time we each gave.

893
00:44:04,893 --> 00:44:08,764
I didn't know how to bring it up.

894
00:44:08,764 --> 00:44:12,768
At the same time, I was shocked...

895
00:44:13,769 --> 00:44:16,104
that he gave me all 100 minutes.

896
00:44:18,540 --> 00:44:20,175
The message showed our times.

897
00:44:20,175 --> 00:44:22,744
I knew how many minutes I'd given,

898
00:44:22,744 --> 00:44:26,381
so I knew how many Ro Bin gave me.

899
00:44:29,351 --> 00:44:31,653
No matter how much time she'd given me,

900
00:44:31,653 --> 00:44:33,789
it didn't matter...

901
00:44:33,789 --> 00:44:34,756
because I'd already...

902
00:44:34,756 --> 00:44:37,826
gotten to go on a date with her.

903
00:44:37,826 --> 00:44:40,362
That was what mattered to me.

904
00:44:42,364 --> 00:44:43,999
- That's impressive.
- As expected.

905
00:44:43,999 --> 00:44:47,202
He gave 100 minutes because he liked her.

906
00:44:47,202 --> 00:44:48,337
What a man.

907
00:44:48,337 --> 00:44:49,738
(Moved)

908
00:44:49,738 --> 00:44:51,206
- A perfect score.
- Seriously.

909
00:44:51,206 --> 00:44:52,708
What do I do?

910
00:44:52,708 --> 00:44:54,142
Why am I the one feeling awkward?

911
00:44:56,345 --> 00:44:57,613
It could be an awkward situation.

912
00:44:57,613 --> 00:44:58,881
Ro Bin may feel embarrassed.

913
00:45:01,717 --> 00:45:05,754
(After receiving the message,
the mood between them shifts.)

914
00:45:11,093 --> 00:45:14,763
I didn't know our exact times
would be revealed.

915
00:45:14,763 --> 00:45:16,732
Me neither.

916
00:45:16,732 --> 00:45:18,467
I thought everything
in that Secret Room...

917
00:45:19,701 --> 00:45:22,538
was something only I knew.

918
00:45:22,538 --> 00:45:24,806
Then the message suddenly revealed it.

919
00:45:24,806 --> 00:45:25,874
So...

920
00:45:26,742 --> 00:45:27,709
I see.

921
00:45:28,810 --> 00:45:32,381
Exactly. I wasn't expecting numbers.

922
00:45:32,381 --> 00:45:33,667
For me, though,

923
00:45:34,416 --> 00:45:36,552
I made that choice...

924
00:45:37,586 --> 00:45:40,322
because I was sure
it would lead to a date.

925
00:45:40,322 --> 00:45:41,423
- Really?
- Yes.

926
00:45:42,825 --> 00:45:45,160
That's why I made that choice.

927
00:45:46,261 --> 00:45:47,196
It's just...

928
00:45:48,096 --> 00:45:50,566
This is what I'm like.

929
00:45:50,566 --> 00:45:53,001
Once I find someone I like,
I become direct.

930
00:45:54,903 --> 00:45:57,739
I never know if another chance will come,
that's why.

931
00:45:59,541 --> 00:46:01,009
Wait, I got a message.

932
00:46:02,978 --> 00:46:08,016
(Seo Ro Bin, your second date is waiting.)

933
00:46:08,016 --> 00:46:10,752
(Please move to the next location.)

934
00:46:11,019 --> 00:46:14,656
My second date is waiting?

935
00:46:14,990 --> 00:46:17,226
I wondered who my second date might be.

936
00:46:17,659 --> 00:46:20,796
Who is it? Who is my second date?

937
00:46:21,029 --> 00:46:22,598
I had no idea.

938
00:46:26,235 --> 00:46:27,503
I...

939
00:46:27,503 --> 00:46:28,403
There's a car coming.

940
00:46:28,737 --> 00:46:29,705
Next,

941
00:46:30,606 --> 00:46:33,642
I need to stop somewhere nearby.

942
00:46:33,642 --> 00:46:35,410
I think I should stop there on the way.

943
00:46:35,410 --> 00:46:36,478
This is where we...

944
00:46:36,478 --> 00:46:37,379
Here?

945
00:46:37,379 --> 00:46:38,914
I think we need to part ways here.

946
00:46:38,914 --> 00:46:42,751
I wished we could keep going together.

947
00:46:43,852 --> 00:46:46,488
I wondered where she was going...

948
00:46:46,989 --> 00:46:49,124
or if she was headed to another date,

949
00:46:49,124 --> 00:46:51,560
I wished I could at least...

950
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:53,929
take her to her next date.

951
00:46:54,563 --> 00:46:56,064
Take her to her next date?

952
00:46:56,665 --> 00:46:57,666
Seriously?

953
00:46:57,666 --> 00:46:58,901
Goodness.

954
00:46:58,901 --> 00:47:01,069
- That's so impressive.
- It really is.

955
00:47:01,069 --> 00:47:02,905
Even at the very end...

956
00:47:02,905 --> 00:47:05,174
He offered to walk her there.

957
00:47:05,174 --> 00:47:06,341
How could he be so thoughtful?

958
00:47:06,341 --> 00:47:07,910
He knew she'd only given him ten minutes.

959
00:47:07,910 --> 00:47:10,612
I'd have sulked a little.

960
00:47:10,612 --> 00:47:12,347
Ten minutes would sting a little.

961
00:47:12,347 --> 00:47:14,049
You're visibly sulking.

962
00:47:14,049 --> 00:47:16,718
I'd have said,
"You only gave me ten minutes."

963
00:47:16,718 --> 00:47:18,487
But he didn't show it at all.

964
00:47:18,487 --> 00:47:19,488
He stayed considerate until the end.

965
00:47:19,488 --> 00:47:20,556
Exactly.

966
00:47:20,556 --> 00:47:22,324
That was so impressive.

967
00:47:22,324 --> 00:47:23,325
He's incredible.

968
00:47:28,764 --> 00:47:30,299
I have to go this way.

969
00:47:30,299 --> 00:47:31,133
Later.

970
00:47:32,034 --> 00:47:33,468
- See you later.
- See you later.

971
00:47:37,005 --> 00:47:41,643
(They part reluctantly.)

972
00:47:43,616 --> 00:47:46,385
(Meanwhile,)

973
00:47:46,385 --> 00:47:48,821
(Jong Eun rests alone.)

974
00:47:50,289 --> 00:47:51,524
Where did everyone go?

975
00:47:54,727 --> 00:47:55,928
Did you eat?

976
00:47:55,928 --> 00:47:56,829
No, not yet.

977
00:47:56,829 --> 00:47:57,897
Why not?

978
00:47:57,897 --> 00:48:00,733
I'm having cucumber with seasoned soybean
and chili paste with porridge.

979
00:48:02,301 --> 00:48:03,469
(Chuckling)

980
00:48:03,469 --> 00:48:05,037
- Are you all right with that?
- Let's go.

981
00:48:05,471 --> 00:48:08,507
Then, let's head to the kitchen first.

982
00:48:09,642 --> 00:48:10,576
(They get to have lunch alone.)

983
00:48:10,576 --> 00:48:11,611
Let's eat.

984
00:48:11,611 --> 00:48:12,678
Enjoy your meal.

985
00:48:12,678 --> 00:48:14,246
What do you think? Do you like cucumber?

986
00:48:14,246 --> 00:48:15,581
I can't eat cucumbers.

987
00:48:15,581 --> 00:48:16,749
Right, I'm sorry.

988
00:48:18,117 --> 00:48:19,252
I forgot you said that.

989
00:48:20,019 --> 00:48:21,754
You said you hate the smell of cucumbers.

990
00:48:21,754 --> 00:48:23,055
Can you smell it now?

991
00:48:23,055 --> 00:48:24,423
No, I'm fine.

992
00:48:24,423 --> 00:48:26,092
Are you sure? Can you smell it?

993
00:48:26,092 --> 00:48:27,260
No, I can't.

994
00:48:28,394 --> 00:48:29,629
(Crunching)

995
00:48:31,597 --> 00:48:32,632
(Laughing)

996
00:48:33,933 --> 00:48:35,234
Is it good with the paste?

997
00:48:35,234 --> 00:48:36,102
Yes.

998
00:48:36,802 --> 00:48:38,204
You never tried it?

999
00:48:38,204 --> 00:48:39,905
Trust me and try just one bite.

1000
00:48:41,907 --> 00:48:43,142
(Thinking)

1001
00:48:43,776 --> 00:48:45,511
This is taking a lot of courage.

1002
00:48:47,980 --> 00:48:49,115
Just one bite.

1003
00:48:50,249 --> 00:48:51,217
Only a tiny one.

1004
00:48:51,217 --> 00:48:52,351
(Min Young breaks his cucumber barrier.)

1005
00:48:52,351 --> 00:48:53,252
Bite it.

1006
00:48:53,252 --> 00:48:54,320
No.

1007
00:48:54,854 --> 00:48:56,289
How is it?

1008
00:48:58,257 --> 00:48:59,759
(Grimacing)

1009
00:49:00,192 --> 00:49:01,260
You aren't going to throw up, right?

1010
00:49:01,260 --> 00:49:02,762
I can't tell what it tastes like.

1011
00:49:02,762 --> 00:49:03,829
Really?

1012
00:49:03,829 --> 00:49:05,231
Do you want to spit it out?

1013
00:49:06,766 --> 00:49:07,633
I'm sorry.

1014
00:49:08,668 --> 00:49:10,102
Don't eat it next time.

1015
00:49:10,102 --> 00:49:11,804
I didn't know you hated it this much.

1016
00:49:11,804 --> 00:49:13,306
Thank you for eating the cucumber.

1017
00:49:14,941 --> 00:49:17,209
- I tried very hard.
- Thank you.

1018
00:49:22,315 --> 00:49:24,750
Do you regret the choice you made...

1019
00:49:25,017 --> 00:49:26,953
in the Room of Time yesterday?

1020
00:49:28,020 --> 00:49:29,322
I don't regret it at all.

1021
00:49:30,222 --> 00:49:31,157
Do you regret yours?

1022
00:49:32,658 --> 00:49:34,160
I don't really regret mine either.

1023
00:49:35,127 --> 00:49:36,329
It was the first day.

1024
00:49:38,731 --> 00:49:40,600
I really like your personality, Min Young.

1025
00:49:40,600 --> 00:49:41,901
- Who?
- Your personality.

1026
00:49:41,901 --> 00:49:42,735
Really?

1027
00:49:42,735 --> 00:49:44,737
People often compliment my personality.

1028
00:49:44,971 --> 00:49:46,939
They compliment it, but never fall for me.

1029
00:49:50,176 --> 00:49:51,344
Someone might.

1030
00:49:52,178 --> 00:49:53,446
They really didn't.

1031
00:49:53,980 --> 00:49:57,249
(Jong Eun subtly reveals his feelings.)

1032
00:49:59,552 --> 00:50:01,887
When do you feel romantic attraction...

1033
00:50:01,887 --> 00:50:03,723
toward someone, Min Young?

1034
00:50:07,360 --> 00:50:08,494
I need to feel a spark.

1035
00:50:10,029 --> 00:50:11,731
I need that spark.
You know what I mean, right?

1036
00:50:12,765 --> 00:50:13,933
What kind of spark?

1037
00:50:13,933 --> 00:50:15,067
I don't know.

1038
00:50:17,036 --> 00:50:19,605
But I never dated anyone I felt drawn to.

1039
00:50:19,605 --> 00:50:20,773
Really?

1040
00:50:21,641 --> 00:50:24,277
Then what's your ideal type?

1041
00:50:24,677 --> 00:50:26,178
Someone who is kind of like a potato.

1042
00:50:27,380 --> 00:50:29,815
He should be happy with what he does.

1043
00:50:30,650 --> 00:50:31,851
My ideal type is a potato,

1044
00:50:31,851 --> 00:50:33,419
but I don't think I've ever met one.

1045
00:50:33,419 --> 00:50:35,721
I've never met my ideal potato.

1046
00:50:36,923 --> 00:50:39,725
Shouldn't you visit Gangwon State, then?

1047
00:50:39,725 --> 00:50:41,193
That's actually true.

1048
00:50:41,193 --> 00:50:44,897
I want someone who seems from the country.

1049
00:50:45,698 --> 00:50:48,501
But the men I dated weren't like that.

1050
00:50:48,501 --> 00:50:50,903
Do I seem like I'd live in the country?

1051
00:50:54,173 --> 00:50:55,107
No.

1052
00:50:55,775 --> 00:50:57,677
- You seem like you belong in Seoul.
- Me?

1053
00:50:59,478 --> 00:51:00,413
Why?

1054
00:51:01,280 --> 00:51:03,215
Jong Eun seems more like a country guy.

1055
00:51:03,215 --> 00:51:06,319
He looks exactly like a country potato.

1056
00:51:06,319 --> 00:51:07,820
He's the potato king.

1057
00:51:08,821 --> 00:51:09,989
(Jong Eun is the ultimate king potato.)

1058
00:51:09,989 --> 00:51:10,957
Isn't he?

1059
00:51:11,791 --> 00:51:14,327
He's the most potato-like of the four.

1060
00:51:14,327 --> 00:51:15,261
He's definitely a potato.

1061
00:51:15,261 --> 00:51:16,696
Completely.

1062
00:51:16,696 --> 00:51:18,764
- A potato is her ideal type.
- Goodness.

1063
00:51:18,764 --> 00:51:20,800
What does she even mean by a potato?

1064
00:51:25,304 --> 00:51:26,739
You don't seem like a country man.

1065
00:51:28,274 --> 00:51:31,444
(Her bar for a country potato is high.)

1066
00:51:32,645 --> 00:51:34,413
(Meanwhile,)

1067
00:51:35,715 --> 00:51:40,186
(Ro Bin waits for her second date.)

1068
00:51:42,154 --> 00:51:45,458
(A mysterious vehicle approaches Ro Bin.)

1069
00:51:46,325 --> 00:51:48,127
What is that?

1070
00:51:52,632 --> 00:51:53,933
You startled me.

1071
00:51:54,567 --> 00:51:56,869
- Good to see you.
- Good to see you.

1072
00:51:58,571 --> 00:51:59,772
Someone suddenly appeared.

1073
00:51:59,772 --> 00:52:00,840
It was Ryun Gi.

1074
00:52:02,808 --> 00:52:04,910
I suddenly thought of "Boys Over Flowers."

1075
00:52:04,910 --> 00:52:06,746
I don't know why.

1076
00:52:06,746 --> 00:52:09,882
I was so happy to see her waiting.

1077
00:52:10,716 --> 00:52:14,186
I'd been hoping she would be my date.

1078
00:52:14,186 --> 00:52:15,655
So I was thrilled.

1079
00:52:16,422 --> 00:52:18,591
- Did you wait long?
- No.

1080
00:52:18,591 --> 00:52:20,693
When did you get here?

1081
00:52:20,693 --> 00:52:22,728
A little while ago.

1082
00:52:24,797 --> 00:52:26,565
Shall we go?
Do you know where we're going?

1083
00:52:26,565 --> 00:52:27,366
I don't.

1084
00:52:27,366 --> 00:52:28,768
- Seriously? You know nothing?
- No.

1085
00:52:28,768 --> 00:52:30,703
- You didn't know I'd come?
- Not at all.

1086
00:52:32,638 --> 00:52:33,806
All right.

1087
00:52:34,507 --> 00:52:35,408
Hop in.

1088
00:52:35,408 --> 00:52:36,642
- Do I get in?
- Yes.

1089
00:52:36,642 --> 00:52:37,843
What?

1090
00:52:37,843 --> 00:52:38,711
Are you opening the door for me?

1091
00:52:38,711 --> 00:52:39,979
Of course.

1092
00:52:39,979 --> 00:52:41,013
Wait.

1093
00:52:41,013 --> 00:52:42,214
I'll open it again from inside.

1094
00:52:42,214 --> 00:52:43,316
Let me open the door.

1095
00:52:43,749 --> 00:52:46,118
(Contrary to what he wanted,
the door is locked.)

1096
00:52:46,118 --> 00:52:47,687
It's locked.

1097
00:52:48,020 --> 00:52:49,755
That makes him even cuter.

1098
00:52:49,755 --> 00:52:51,123
He's cute.

1099
00:52:51,958 --> 00:52:52,959
Ro...

1100
00:52:53,793 --> 00:52:54,694
Ro Bin.

1101
00:52:54,694 --> 00:52:56,762
She's wearing her first-date outfit.

1102
00:52:56,762 --> 00:52:57,597
Right.

1103
00:52:58,831 --> 00:53:00,199
He isn't supposed to know that.

1104
00:53:01,567 --> 00:53:02,668
I'll open the door.

1105
00:53:05,237 --> 00:53:06,505
(Press)

1106
00:53:07,807 --> 00:53:09,241
- Get in.
- All right.

1107
00:53:10,977 --> 00:53:14,947
(Ryun Gi and Ro Bin's
100-minute date begins.)

1108
00:53:20,453 --> 00:53:22,688
(Naksan Park)

1109
00:53:22,688 --> 00:53:24,724
- Are we getting out?
- Yes, go ahead.

1110
00:53:25,524 --> 00:53:26,325
It must've been hard.

1111
00:53:26,325 --> 00:53:29,795
I didn't do anything.
You did all the work.

1112
00:53:31,397 --> 00:53:32,698
Isn't this a nice neighborhood?

1113
00:53:32,698 --> 00:53:33,966
Very.

1114
00:53:33,966 --> 00:53:36,669
I really love little alleys like these.

1115
00:53:37,603 --> 00:53:38,537
Absolutely.

1116
00:53:39,572 --> 00:53:40,873
Wait.

1117
00:53:45,077 --> 00:53:46,412
I think it was this way.

1118
00:53:47,346 --> 00:53:48,447
This way?

1119
00:53:50,216 --> 00:53:51,217
Was it here?

1120
00:53:51,784 --> 00:53:52,985
Here?

1121
00:53:52,985 --> 00:53:53,920
Wait.

1122
00:53:53,920 --> 00:53:56,989
Take your time.

1123
00:53:56,989 --> 00:53:59,759
It's so beautiful wherever we go.

1124
00:54:01,661 --> 00:54:04,897
(They try to find their way.)

1125
00:54:04,897 --> 00:54:06,832
Right. It isn't here.

1126
00:54:07,833 --> 00:54:08,935
Is the name funny?

1127
00:54:08,935 --> 00:54:11,671
No, it's just that the name is so...

1128
00:54:11,671 --> 00:54:13,806
like you, Ryun Gi.

1129
00:54:14,507 --> 00:54:15,408
Is that how I come across?

1130
00:54:15,408 --> 00:54:16,809
No, that's not quite what I mean.

1131
00:54:18,077 --> 00:54:22,415
Do I come off as funny in the house?

1132
00:54:22,415 --> 00:54:23,349
Do I seem like a funny person?

1133
00:54:23,349 --> 00:54:26,052
No, you don't. It's more your...

1134
00:54:26,052 --> 00:54:27,286
presence.

1135
00:54:27,286 --> 00:54:28,421
My presence?

1136
00:54:29,422 --> 00:54:30,890
You mean it in a good way, right?

1137
00:54:30,890 --> 00:54:31,958
Absolutely.

1138
00:54:31,958 --> 00:54:32,825
What a relief.

1139
00:54:32,825 --> 00:54:33,960
You're someone everyone needs.

1140
00:54:35,461 --> 00:54:37,830
Can you really praise me that much?

1141
00:54:39,432 --> 00:54:40,399
Yes.

1142
00:54:40,399 --> 00:54:41,701
That's very high praise.

1143
00:54:41,701 --> 00:54:44,203
Is it? I guess it is.

1144
00:54:45,671 --> 00:54:47,273
This street is really beautiful.

1145
00:54:47,273 --> 00:54:48,074
Right?

1146
00:54:48,908 --> 00:54:50,409
It's such a beautiful street.

1147
00:54:51,277 --> 00:54:54,213
Let's sit over there.

1148
00:54:54,213 --> 00:54:55,748
Where we can see better.

1149
00:54:55,748 --> 00:54:58,217
(They reach today's date location.)

1150
00:54:59,118 --> 00:55:01,220
It would be stunning in nicer weather.

1151
00:55:01,220 --> 00:55:03,723
But it's already beautiful.

1152
00:55:03,723 --> 00:55:04,757
Sit here.

1153
00:55:04,757 --> 00:55:06,325
You're such a gentleman.

1154
00:55:07,293 --> 00:55:08,261
Amazing.

1155
00:55:09,528 --> 00:55:11,597
The view from here is beautiful.

1156
00:55:11,597 --> 00:55:14,133
I've wanted to come somewhere high up.

1157
00:55:15,668 --> 00:55:16,902
It really is beautiful.

1158
00:55:17,270 --> 00:55:19,238
If you keep looking out,

1159
00:55:19,238 --> 00:55:21,107
it makes you feel refreshed.

1160
00:55:21,107 --> 00:55:22,541
Exactly. That's the feeling.

1161
00:55:22,541 --> 00:55:23,476
A sense of freedom.

1162
00:55:23,476 --> 00:55:25,578
Yes, I feel so refreshed right now.

1163
00:55:28,914 --> 00:55:31,651
The reason I wanted to come here...

1164
00:55:32,618 --> 00:55:35,388
is that wherever I go with someone,

1165
00:55:35,388 --> 00:55:38,024
I always seem to remember...

1166
00:55:38,024 --> 00:55:39,926
the scenery around us too.

1167
00:55:39,926 --> 00:55:40,893
Really?

1168
00:55:40,893 --> 00:55:43,930
If I remember a beautiful place...

1169
00:55:43,930 --> 00:55:47,566
along with the person beside me,

1170
00:55:47,566 --> 00:55:49,068
I think that would be wonderful.

1171
00:55:50,536 --> 00:55:53,973
I'm different. I only see the person.

1172
00:55:53,973 --> 00:55:55,474
The background disappears for me.

1173
00:55:56,208 --> 00:55:57,209
You get completely absorbed?

1174
00:55:57,209 --> 00:55:59,211
Yes, completely.

1175
00:55:59,211 --> 00:56:00,379
I'm the immersive type.

1176
00:56:00,379 --> 00:56:01,647
This is all I see.

1177
00:56:01,647 --> 00:56:05,117
You're really good at making eye contact.

1178
00:56:05,117 --> 00:56:06,986
That's really...

1179
00:56:06,986 --> 00:56:08,154
Am I?

1180
00:56:08,154 --> 00:56:10,556
Actually, yesterday,

1181
00:56:12,124 --> 00:56:13,492
I noticed...

1182
00:56:14,026 --> 00:56:16,295
how well you held eye contact.

1183
00:56:16,629 --> 00:56:17,930
The two of us?

1184
00:56:17,930 --> 00:56:19,065
Right.

1185
00:56:19,065 --> 00:56:21,000
And for me,

1186
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:23,002
even without saying anything,

1187
00:56:23,002 --> 00:56:25,204
that simple gesture...

1188
00:56:25,204 --> 00:56:27,173
made me feel grateful and happy.

1189
00:56:27,673 --> 00:56:30,943
So you made a great first impression.

1190
00:56:30,943 --> 00:56:33,546
You weren't the only one. I felt it too.

1191
00:56:33,546 --> 00:56:34,981
Really?

1192
00:56:34,981 --> 00:56:36,816
Didn't we keep making eye contact?

1193
00:56:36,816 --> 00:56:38,150
- Exactly.
- Right?

1194
00:56:38,451 --> 00:56:41,721
We looked while other people were talking.

1195
00:56:41,721 --> 00:56:43,022
But I wondered...

1196
00:56:43,022 --> 00:56:46,592
if you were looking at Seon Ho.

1197
00:56:46,592 --> 00:56:47,493
You were looking at me?

1198
00:56:47,960 --> 00:56:49,161
(Nodding)

1199
00:56:51,030 --> 00:56:52,365
What?

1200
00:56:53,332 --> 00:56:54,500
Ro Bin is saying all of that now.

1201
00:56:54,500 --> 00:56:56,636
What if her ten minutes come out later?

1202
00:56:58,471 --> 00:57:00,273
(Ro Bin gave Ryun Gi 10 minutes.)

1203
00:57:00,273 --> 00:57:02,041
- It was only ten minutes, Ro Bin.
- Right.

1204
00:57:02,041 --> 00:57:03,309
Watch what you say, Ro Bin.

1205
00:57:03,309 --> 00:57:05,578
You sound like you gave him 50 minutes.

1206
00:57:05,578 --> 00:57:07,179
Now I'm getting nervous again.

1207
00:57:08,014 --> 00:57:09,181
(Watching closely)

1208
00:57:11,350 --> 00:57:13,686
I'm so curious about your age and job.

1209
00:57:13,686 --> 00:57:16,822
I think you're younger than me.

1210
00:57:16,822 --> 00:57:17,690
Me?

1211
00:57:18,524 --> 00:57:19,525
Really?

1212
00:57:22,128 --> 00:57:23,329
Did I act too young?

1213
00:57:23,329 --> 00:57:26,565
No, you just seem playful and sweet.

1214
00:57:27,667 --> 00:57:28,834
So maybe.

1215
00:57:30,069 --> 00:57:31,804
But I'm a very masculine man.

1216
00:57:32,204 --> 00:57:33,472
I mean,

1217
00:57:33,472 --> 00:57:36,776
I never said I dislike playful people.

1218
00:57:38,611 --> 00:57:40,246
But men have this thing.

1219
00:57:40,246 --> 00:57:42,281
They don't want to seem too young.

1220
00:57:42,281 --> 00:57:44,050
- Really?
- As a man, you know.

1221
00:57:50,523 --> 00:57:51,557
(Staring)

1222
00:57:52,892 --> 00:57:53,826
Come here.

1223
00:57:53,826 --> 00:57:55,461
There's something in your hair.

1224
00:57:57,897 --> 00:57:58,831
Thank you.

1225
00:58:02,735 --> 00:58:06,672
Men usually dislike being the younger one.

1226
00:58:06,672 --> 00:58:08,841
Really?

1227
00:58:08,841 --> 00:58:10,009
I'm sorry.

1228
00:58:10,009 --> 00:58:12,211
No, that's not what I meant.

1229
00:58:13,446 --> 00:58:17,416
I don't think age matters much to me.

1230
00:58:17,984 --> 00:58:19,318
(Nodding)

1231
00:58:25,591 --> 00:58:26,993
(Slurping)

1232
00:58:29,462 --> 00:58:30,696
Am I drinking too fast?

1233
00:58:31,697 --> 00:58:33,633
Cold drinks are meant to be gulped.

1234
00:58:35,835 --> 00:58:37,103
I should drink more slowly.

1235
00:58:38,671 --> 00:58:40,940
- I can't drink cold things quickly.
- Right.

1236
00:58:43,876 --> 00:58:47,246
It took me a long time to change that.

1237
00:58:47,246 --> 00:58:48,314
Really?

1238
00:58:48,314 --> 00:58:49,982
Eating is a habit, after all.

1239
00:58:49,982 --> 00:58:51,450
I suppose so.

1240
00:58:52,251 --> 00:58:54,954
If I gulp it without thinking...

1241
00:58:56,622 --> 00:58:57,723
Exactly.

1242
00:58:59,959 --> 00:59:01,227
What do you think?

1243
00:59:01,227 --> 00:59:04,697
We haven't spent that much time together,

1244
00:59:04,697 --> 00:59:09,302
but do you think you and I...

1245
00:59:10,002 --> 00:59:11,871
have some things in common?

1246
00:59:13,472 --> 00:59:16,042
Of course. We have plenty in common.

1247
00:59:16,042 --> 00:59:18,945
Didn't you feel it while we were talking?

1248
00:59:18,945 --> 00:59:21,280
We definitely have things in common.

1249
00:59:22,315 --> 00:59:26,118
I'm being completely honest right now.

1250
00:59:28,187 --> 00:59:32,892
To be honest, someone like you, Ro Bin...

1251
00:59:32,892 --> 00:59:36,329
Although I don't know you very well yet,

1252
00:59:40,299 --> 00:59:44,170
you seem close to my ideal type.

1253
00:59:44,170 --> 00:59:45,237
Really?

1254
00:59:45,871 --> 00:59:49,275
I loved how you made eye contact with me.

1255
00:59:49,275 --> 00:59:52,745
I liked all those little gestures.

1256
00:59:52,745 --> 00:59:54,213
I see.

1257
00:59:55,181 --> 00:59:56,148
(Shy)

1258
00:59:57,183 --> 00:59:58,451
(Sneaks a glance)

1259
00:59:59,919 --> 01:00:00,920
Thank you.

1260
01:00:02,655 --> 01:00:04,924
You're so honest.

1261
01:00:05,658 --> 01:00:06,726
Thank you so much.

1262
01:00:25,244 --> 01:00:26,078
What is it?

1263
01:00:27,913 --> 01:00:30,349
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

1264
01:00:30,349 --> 01:00:35,821
(Kim Ryun Gi and Seo Ro Bin,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

1265
01:00:36,789 --> 01:00:38,391
(Flustered)

1266
01:00:42,461 --> 01:00:46,232
(Ryun Gi, 90 minutes / Ro Bin, 10 minutes)

1267
01:00:46,699 --> 01:00:50,236
(As the date ends,
they realize their feelings don't align.)

1268
01:00:53,239 --> 01:00:54,173
I wish we had more time.

1269
01:00:54,173 --> 01:00:55,641
Me too.

1270
01:00:55,641 --> 01:00:56,542
Are you sad it's over?

1271
01:00:57,543 --> 01:00:58,344
Very.

1272
01:00:58,344 --> 01:00:59,211
Sorry.

1273
01:01:00,179 --> 01:01:01,113
Do you really mean that?

1274
01:01:01,113 --> 01:01:02,281
I can't lie.

1275
01:01:08,788 --> 01:01:13,159
When the message revealed our choices...

1276
01:01:13,159 --> 01:01:16,062
and how much time we'd given each other,

1277
01:01:16,295 --> 01:01:19,799
I wondered what her ten minutes meant.

1278
01:01:19,799 --> 01:01:22,568
I didn't expect it, but I kept thinking.

1279
01:01:22,568 --> 01:01:25,137
That was what I wanted to ask most.

1280
01:01:25,137 --> 01:01:28,174
- How could he not wonder?
- It stays with you.

1281
01:01:28,174 --> 01:01:29,809
You can't help it.

1282
01:01:29,809 --> 01:01:32,511
The mood subtly shifted after the message.

1283
01:01:33,379 --> 01:01:34,647
It's all right.

1284
01:01:35,481 --> 01:01:36,482
Ryun Gi.

1285
01:01:38,084 --> 01:01:41,520
(On the way back to the House)

1286
01:01:43,122 --> 01:01:44,223
Cool.

1287
01:01:47,760 --> 01:01:52,832
(The car is quiet, unlike before.)

1288
01:01:56,068 --> 01:01:57,770
I wanted to ask you about that earlier.

1289
01:01:57,770 --> 01:01:58,804
Actually...

1290
01:02:01,007 --> 01:02:02,208
You got the text, right?

1291
01:02:03,309 --> 01:02:05,211
It said...

1292
01:02:05,211 --> 01:02:09,882
our date ended
because we chose a total of 100 minutes.

1293
01:02:10,449 --> 01:02:12,184
What that really means is this.

1294
01:02:12,184 --> 01:02:14,453
You now know how much time you gave,

1295
01:02:14,453 --> 01:02:16,589
and how much the other person gave.

1296
01:02:18,291 --> 01:02:20,026
Can I ask you about it?

1297
01:02:20,026 --> 01:02:20,927
About what?

1298
01:02:20,927 --> 01:02:22,995
What did those ten minutes mean?

1299
01:02:23,773 --> 01:02:24,974
For me,

1300
01:02:26,309 --> 01:02:29,512
what I heard yesterday weighed on me.

1301
01:02:29,746 --> 01:02:33,116
Listening to your
battle-against-illness diary,

1302
01:02:33,383 --> 01:02:37,620
I realized you're still going through it.

1303
01:02:37,620 --> 01:02:42,659
When I pictured what that might mean,

1304
01:02:42,659 --> 01:02:45,461
I thought about how, in a relationship,

1305
01:02:45,461 --> 01:02:50,900
I don't want my partner
to be the only one...

1306
01:02:51,467 --> 01:02:57,073
who has to make accommodations for me.

1307
01:02:57,073 --> 01:03:00,443
You mean having them accommodate you?

1308
01:03:00,443 --> 01:03:03,913
I believe both people should compromise.

1309
01:03:03,913 --> 01:03:08,785
But I worried there might be things
I wouldn't be able to compromise on.

1310
01:03:08,785 --> 01:03:10,887
When I considered that,

1311
01:03:10,887 --> 01:03:15,425
that gave me a lot to think about,
and I felt I needed more time.

1312
01:03:18,027 --> 01:03:19,562
I had even more on my mind.

1313
01:03:19,562 --> 01:03:22,832
I was still really grateful...

1314
01:03:22,832 --> 01:03:25,401
that she gave me even ten minutes.

1315
01:03:25,401 --> 01:03:27,704
It wasn't so much disappointment.

1316
01:03:27,704 --> 01:03:32,008
I just didn't expect my biggest concern
to become reality so quickly.

1317
01:03:32,008 --> 01:03:33,977
So it threw me.

1318
01:03:37,080 --> 01:03:39,449
For me, too,

1319
01:03:40,483 --> 01:03:43,319
I keep becoming more cautious.

1320
01:03:43,319 --> 01:03:45,588
I feel bad for the other person...

1321
01:03:45,588 --> 01:03:46,756
and start feeling guilty.

1322
01:03:47,490 --> 01:03:50,059
I've been thinking the same thing.

1323
01:03:51,661 --> 01:03:53,530
Because you feel bad?

1324
01:03:54,097 --> 01:03:57,567
I feel like they'd have to adapt to me...

1325
01:03:57,567 --> 01:03:59,369
and give certain things up...

1326
01:03:59,369 --> 01:04:01,838
because of me.

1327
01:04:01,838 --> 01:04:03,907
Right now, that's still...

1328
01:04:04,908 --> 01:04:09,312
a part of myself I struggle to open up.

1329
01:04:09,312 --> 01:04:12,282
I was very guarded before coming here.

1330
01:04:13,716 --> 01:04:15,652
That's why, honestly,

1331
01:04:16,386 --> 01:04:17,287
I think that's the difference.

1332
01:04:17,287 --> 01:04:19,289
I'm still going through it,

1333
01:04:19,289 --> 01:04:22,992
unlike the others who've recovered.

1334
01:04:22,992 --> 01:04:24,460
It affects your outlook.

1335
01:04:25,495 --> 01:04:29,465
I tried my best to set that aside,

1336
01:04:29,465 --> 01:04:32,235
but I thought about it a lot yesterday.

1337
01:04:33,436 --> 01:04:35,805
I really agonized over it.

1338
01:04:35,805 --> 01:04:36,806
I really did.

1339
01:04:37,307 --> 01:04:38,908
I thought about it so much.

1340
01:04:38,908 --> 01:04:40,009
Still, thank you.

1341
01:04:42,478 --> 01:04:47,050
When I pictured us dating later,

1342
01:04:47,050 --> 01:04:49,185
I thought there would be
a lot of things...

1343
01:04:49,185 --> 01:04:51,788
I'd constantly have to accommodate.

1344
01:04:52,288 --> 01:04:55,325
He drank cold drinks really slowly.

1345
01:04:55,325 --> 01:04:58,828
And I hadn't even noticed that.

1346
01:04:58,828 --> 01:05:02,332
I felt bad for overlooking it.

1347
01:05:02,332 --> 01:05:03,900
Things like that kept making me think...

1348
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:06,369
about the ways I'd have to adjust.

1349
01:05:06,369 --> 01:05:09,506
I wondered if it might be hard for me.

1350
01:05:11,774 --> 01:05:15,044
When I hear something like that now,

1351
01:05:15,044 --> 01:05:18,381
I still feel a little helpless.

1352
01:05:18,381 --> 01:05:21,951
No matter what I say in that moment,

1353
01:05:21,951 --> 01:05:25,154
once the other person starts worrying,

1354
01:05:25,154 --> 01:05:27,757
I can't make it go away with words.

1355
01:05:27,757 --> 01:05:30,860
I was also afraid my struggles...

1356
01:05:30,860 --> 01:05:32,529
would rub off on someone close to me.

1357
01:05:33,463 --> 01:05:36,065
- This is so hard.
- This is truly heartbreaking.

1358
01:05:37,534 --> 01:05:39,702
From Ryun Gi's perspective,

1359
01:05:39,702 --> 01:05:41,704
"Then what am I supposed to do?"

1360
01:05:41,704 --> 01:05:42,605
That's probably how he feels.

1361
01:05:42,605 --> 01:05:45,108
He can't fix the problem himself.

1362
01:05:45,108 --> 01:05:47,277
He likes her so much,

1363
01:05:47,277 --> 01:05:48,545
but if this is how she feels,

1364
01:05:48,811 --> 01:05:51,147
"Then what am I supposed to do?"

1365
01:05:51,147 --> 01:05:53,183
"What will happen to my love life?"

1366
01:05:53,449 --> 01:05:54,584
I think that's how he must feel.

1367
01:05:55,351 --> 01:05:57,520
But Ro Bin feels that way...

1368
01:05:57,520 --> 01:06:00,023
because she's afraid
she won't support him enough,

1369
01:06:00,023 --> 01:06:02,358
and she feels bad about that.

1370
01:06:02,358 --> 01:06:04,727
That's what makes this hit even harder...

1371
01:06:04,727 --> 01:06:06,429
and feel even sadder.

1372
01:06:07,530 --> 01:06:09,632
This is so difficult.

1373
01:06:09,632 --> 01:06:11,968
(They confront a real-life obstacle.)

1374
01:06:12,735 --> 01:06:17,106
(Can they add more time together?)

1375
01:06:18,041 --> 01:06:19,809
(Meanwhile, at the House)

1376
01:06:20,310 --> 01:06:23,413
I wonder if it's okay
to walk in like this.

1377
01:06:23,413 --> 01:06:25,815
It's so obvious.

1378
01:06:30,286 --> 01:06:32,155
I'm back.

1379
01:06:32,155 --> 01:06:33,957
I haven't eaten a single meal.

1380
01:06:34,190 --> 01:06:35,458
(Surprised)

1381
01:06:35,458 --> 01:06:36,593
You're back.

1382
01:06:36,593 --> 01:06:39,863
We were about to shop and start cooking.

1383
01:06:39,863 --> 01:06:42,098
Really? Are you going
grocery shopping now?

1384
01:06:43,233 --> 01:06:44,567
I see.

1385
01:06:46,436 --> 01:06:47,570
Did you have fun?

1386
01:06:48,338 --> 01:06:49,305
Yes.

1387
01:06:49,305 --> 01:06:50,373
Really?

1388
01:06:50,373 --> 01:06:52,775
I just wish we'd gotten to eat.

1389
01:06:53,443 --> 01:06:54,811
What did you do?

1390
01:06:54,811 --> 01:06:56,646
We went to Haebangchon near Namsan Tower.

1391
01:06:56,646 --> 01:06:59,015
It was my first time in Haebangchon.

1392
01:06:59,015 --> 01:07:02,051
- We had gelato.
- My goodness.

1393
01:07:02,051 --> 01:07:04,220
Then we went to a bookstore...

1394
01:07:04,220 --> 01:07:05,255
and spent some time there.

1395
01:07:05,255 --> 01:07:07,156
Then we were told, "Your date is over."

1396
01:07:10,960 --> 01:07:11,861
Did it make your heart flutter?

1397
01:07:12,962 --> 01:07:14,330
That's what we want to know most.

1398
01:07:14,998 --> 01:07:18,201
Going on a date really does...

1399
01:07:18,201 --> 01:07:19,435
Change things?

1400
01:07:19,435 --> 01:07:20,270
Seriously.

1401
01:07:20,270 --> 01:07:21,538
Well, for now,

1402
01:07:21,538 --> 01:07:23,273
I'll need some time...

1403
01:07:23,273 --> 01:07:24,941
to think about it.

1404
01:07:24,941 --> 01:07:26,276
(Ye Ji freezes up from embarrassment.)

1405
01:07:26,276 --> 01:07:27,610
This is really...

1406
01:07:28,278 --> 01:07:31,414
This is why
you need to talk one-on-one too.

1407
01:07:34,117 --> 01:07:37,921
(Meanwhile,
Seon Ho is alone in the kitchen.)

1408
01:07:43,726 --> 01:07:45,228
Seon Ho.

1409
01:07:45,228 --> 01:07:46,296
Seon Ho.

1410
01:07:47,730 --> 01:07:48,765
Yes?

1411
01:07:52,735 --> 01:07:54,003
Would you like to go grocery shopping?

1412
01:07:54,003 --> 01:07:54,804
Sure.

1413
01:07:54,804 --> 01:07:55,638
Really?

1414
01:07:55,638 --> 01:07:57,774
- Yes, I don't mind.
- All right.

1415
01:07:58,308 --> 01:07:59,409
When are you leaving?

1416
01:07:59,409 --> 01:08:02,045
Soon. I figured you hadn't eaten yet.

1417
01:08:02,045 --> 01:08:03,313
We were going to go on our own,

1418
01:08:03,313 --> 01:08:04,814
but I thought it'd be nice if you came.

1419
01:08:04,814 --> 01:08:05,815
Sure, I'll come with you.

1420
01:08:05,815 --> 01:08:06,783
You're not too tired, are you?

1421
01:08:06,783 --> 01:08:07,851
No, I'm fine.

1422
01:08:09,786 --> 01:08:13,489
He'd just gone on a date with his pick,

1423
01:08:13,489 --> 01:08:15,625
so I thought he might not want to come.

1424
01:08:15,625 --> 01:08:19,362
But he readily agreed to shop with us.

1425
01:08:20,430 --> 01:08:22,198
I thought we might get a little closer.

1426
01:08:24,267 --> 01:08:28,838
(Meanwhile, Ye Ji comes down
to the dining room alone.)

1427
01:08:31,841 --> 01:08:36,312
(She makes do with a quick meal.)

1428
01:08:39,749 --> 01:08:41,017
Enjoy your meal.

1429
01:08:44,320 --> 01:08:49,259
(She sees Seon Ho leaving
to shop with the others.)

1430
01:08:51,060 --> 01:08:54,197
Deep down, I'd hoped Seon Ho and I...

1431
01:08:54,197 --> 01:08:55,899
could stay behind and talk.

1432
01:08:55,899 --> 01:08:57,400
That's what I was thinking,

1433
01:08:57,400 --> 01:08:58,535
but we completely missed each other.

1434
01:08:58,535 --> 01:09:01,538
So I sat there eating alone,

1435
01:09:01,538 --> 01:09:02,672
wondering, "What just happened?"

1436
01:09:04,107 --> 01:09:06,276
(Ye Ji had hoped to spend time
with Seon Ho.)

1437
01:09:06,276 --> 01:09:08,778
(But she eats alone.)

1438
01:09:09,045 --> 01:09:10,747
Poor Ye Ji.

1439
01:09:10,747 --> 01:09:11,881
(Poor thing)

1440
01:09:12,615 --> 01:09:14,584
This is bothering me so much.

1441
01:09:16,252 --> 01:09:17,954
Wait, that just hurt me.

1442
01:09:18,428 --> 01:09:19,589
That stung a little.

1443
01:09:19,589 --> 01:09:21,224
I'm totally crushed too.

1444
01:09:21,224 --> 01:09:22,525
From Ye Ji's perspective,

1445
01:09:22,525 --> 01:09:25,595
someone who knows her past is right there.

1446
01:09:25,595 --> 01:09:26,362
Yes.

1447
01:09:26,362 --> 01:09:29,999
She has so many reasons to call it fate.

1448
01:09:29,999 --> 01:09:32,669
- Her feelings must've soared.
- She came back like that,

1449
01:09:33,336 --> 01:09:34,304
and then, suddenly,

1450
01:09:35,071 --> 01:09:37,073
- "Enjoy your meal."
- Wait.

1451
01:09:37,073 --> 01:09:39,375
He suddenly became so cold.

1452
01:09:39,375 --> 01:09:41,544
She must be so confused.

1453
01:09:41,544 --> 01:09:43,446
"Enjoy your meal."

1454
01:09:43,446 --> 01:09:44,747
That would be disappointing.

1455
01:09:44,747 --> 01:09:46,249
I can't watch this.

1456
01:09:46,249 --> 01:09:47,183
It's giving me a headache.

1457
01:09:47,617 --> 01:09:48,484
Let's go.

1458
01:09:48,484 --> 01:09:51,421
We have a menu planned for today.

1459
01:09:51,421 --> 01:09:53,156
We're making gnocchi and...

1460
01:09:53,156 --> 01:09:54,290
Korean food? Did we settle on Korean?

1461
01:09:54,290 --> 01:09:55,391
I think it'll be fine.

1462
01:09:55,391 --> 01:09:58,127
- Some people might not like...
- Western food.

1463
01:09:58,127 --> 01:10:00,129
Walking backward is so scary.

1464
01:10:00,129 --> 01:10:01,397
The gnocchi was so good.

1465
01:10:01,397 --> 01:10:03,433
What if people ask us for seconds?

1466
01:10:03,433 --> 01:10:05,034
That could be a problem.

1467
01:10:05,034 --> 01:10:06,669
Where did you get the recipe?

1468
01:10:06,669 --> 01:10:08,204
I looked it up.

1469
01:10:08,204 --> 01:10:09,405
I'll show you.

1470
01:10:10,707 --> 01:10:13,042
Do you come to Seoul often?

1471
01:10:13,376 --> 01:10:15,545
No, not often.

1472
01:10:15,545 --> 01:10:18,381
I used to come all the time
for the hospital,

1473
01:10:18,381 --> 01:10:19,749
but my treatment is over now.

1474
01:10:19,749 --> 01:10:21,417
I hardly have any reason to visit Seoul.

1475
01:10:22,552 --> 01:10:24,254
Did you get some sleep?

1476
01:10:24,254 --> 01:10:26,856
How was it? I honestly...

1477
01:10:27,891 --> 01:10:30,527
My eyes were definitely closed, but...

1478
01:10:30,527 --> 01:10:31,728
But you could hear everything.

1479
01:10:31,728 --> 01:10:32,862
I heard it all.

1480
01:10:32,862 --> 01:10:34,831
- Are you a homebody?
- Yes, I am.

1481
01:10:34,831 --> 01:10:36,432
- A total homebody?
- Pretty much.

1482
01:10:37,200 --> 01:10:38,568
What do you do at home?

1483
01:10:38,568 --> 01:10:40,403
I watch anime...

1484
01:10:40,403 --> 01:10:41,871
and cook for myself.

1485
01:10:42,739 --> 01:10:44,641
Look, a golden retriever.

1486
01:10:44,641 --> 01:10:45,508
Isn't it adorable?

1487
01:10:45,875 --> 01:10:48,011
(Hello)

1488
01:10:49,245 --> 01:10:50,246
What should we buy?

1489
01:10:50,246 --> 01:10:51,281
Let me look it up.

1490
01:10:53,449 --> 01:10:57,253
(Meanwhile, at the House)

1491
01:11:01,291 --> 01:11:06,896
(Ye Ji takes something out
while she's alone.)

1492
01:11:14,938 --> 01:11:21,144
(She reads Seon Ho's handwritten page
for a long time.)

1493
01:11:23,980 --> 01:11:26,349
(Fidgeting)

1494
01:11:32,422 --> 01:11:34,524
(1 hour later)

1495
01:11:35,458 --> 01:11:38,828
I do know how to make
spicy braised chicken.

1496
01:11:38,828 --> 01:11:41,197
Should we start cooking right away?

1497
01:11:41,197 --> 01:11:42,165
I guess we should.

1498
01:11:43,499 --> 01:11:44,801
We're back.

1499
01:11:44,801 --> 01:11:46,769
- Hey.
- What were you doing?

1500
01:11:46,769 --> 01:11:48,805
I was just resting.

1501
01:11:49,439 --> 01:11:52,976
We decided to make
spicy braised chicken and sides.

1502
01:11:52,976 --> 01:11:55,278
Come down if you want.
Otherwise, you can keep resting.

1503
01:12:04,921 --> 01:12:08,124
Do you know how to do this?
How do we stir-fry it?

1504
01:12:09,592 --> 01:12:10,527
(Takes one)

1505
01:12:15,164 --> 01:12:16,366
(Tap, tap)

1506
01:12:16,366 --> 01:12:19,135
(The two prepare a rolled omelet.)

1507
01:12:20,236 --> 01:12:21,504
No.

1508
01:12:21,504 --> 01:12:22,739
Why?

1509
01:12:22,739 --> 01:12:24,607
(A piece of eggshell fell in.)

1510
01:12:28,211 --> 01:12:29,045
Hold on.

1511
01:12:29,279 --> 01:12:30,246
Did I do that?

1512
01:12:30,246 --> 01:12:31,247
I did it.

1513
01:12:43,259 --> 01:12:44,394
(Close together)

1514
01:12:45,795 --> 01:12:49,199
(The distance between them closes.)

1515
01:12:50,533 --> 01:12:52,335
- There.
- Got it.

1516
01:13:01,811 --> 01:13:03,279
Hello.

1517
01:13:03,980 --> 01:13:07,217
(Ye Ji comes into the kitchen.)

1518
01:13:08,551 --> 01:13:09,719
Do we need to make rice?

1519
01:13:09,719 --> 01:13:10,720
Yes.

1520
01:13:11,387 --> 01:13:13,122
Will you help us make the rice?

1521
01:13:13,122 --> 01:13:14,090
I'd love that.

1522
01:13:16,159 --> 01:13:17,427
(Grabs it)

1523
01:13:18,027 --> 01:13:19,362
That startled me.

1524
01:13:19,362 --> 01:13:20,530
Take it slow.

1525
01:13:22,498 --> 01:13:24,500
(Glances over)

1526
01:13:32,542 --> 01:13:33,343
(Laughs)

1527
01:13:34,177 --> 01:13:37,347
(Min Young keeps watching Seon Ho.)

1528
01:13:37,347 --> 01:13:38,481
You're really good at this.

1529
01:13:38,481 --> 01:13:39,449
You make a great rolled omelet.

1530
01:13:39,449 --> 01:13:42,785
I'm just worried about the seasoning.

1531
01:13:43,820 --> 01:13:44,654
You're good.

1532
01:13:46,623 --> 01:13:49,893
(She hears the two talking nearby.)

1533
01:13:51,895 --> 01:13:55,498
The people who went
grocery shopping today...

1534
01:13:55,498 --> 01:13:58,701
seemed to have gotten really close.

1535
01:13:58,701 --> 01:14:00,570
So I was really confused.

1536
01:14:00,570 --> 01:14:03,173
I thought the date had gone well,

1537
01:14:03,606 --> 01:14:04,908
so what was happening?

1538
01:14:04,908 --> 01:14:06,543
Had I imagined the whole thing?

1539
01:14:06,876 --> 01:14:07,810
Goodness.

1540
01:14:07,810 --> 01:14:09,612
No.

1541
01:14:09,612 --> 01:14:11,581
This is driving me crazy.

1542
01:14:12,849 --> 01:14:14,050
She's sitting in the worst possible spot.

1543
01:14:18,788 --> 01:14:23,493
(Complicated feelings begin to tangle.)

1544
01:14:29,999 --> 01:14:32,168
We're eating pretty late.

1545
01:14:32,168 --> 01:14:34,938
(Meanwhile, Ryun Gi and Ro Bin return.)

1546
01:14:35,171 --> 01:14:36,439
Is everyone upstairs?

1547
01:14:36,973 --> 01:14:40,276
(Dinner preparations are in full swing.)

1548
01:14:40,977 --> 01:14:46,282
(Chef Jong Eun's confident creation,
gnocchi, is ready.)

1549
01:14:47,517 --> 01:14:51,054
(Do Gon heads downstairs
after hearing the commotion.)

1550
01:14:51,454 --> 01:14:53,022
- Have you eaten?
- Dinner?

1551
01:14:53,022 --> 01:14:54,524
We want to eat a bit too.

1552
01:14:54,524 --> 01:14:55,658
- Really? Good.
- I'll have some too.

1553
01:14:55,658 --> 01:14:56,626
We have way too much.

1554
01:14:56,626 --> 01:14:58,127
I want some too.

1555
01:14:58,127 --> 01:14:59,262
Have some.

1556
01:14:59,262 --> 01:15:00,296
When did you get back?

1557
01:15:00,296 --> 01:15:01,431
I...

1558
01:15:01,431 --> 01:15:03,199
got back a little while ago.

1559
01:15:03,199 --> 01:15:04,567
I was upstairs.

1560
01:15:04,567 --> 01:15:05,969
Then I came down.

1561
01:15:05,969 --> 01:15:08,371
Amazing, right? Chef Jong Eun made it.

1562
01:15:08,771 --> 01:15:10,039
This is incredible.

1563
01:15:10,039 --> 01:15:11,407
What? Who made this?

1564
01:15:11,774 --> 01:15:13,076
What is this? Is it gnocchi?

1565
01:15:13,076 --> 01:15:14,010
Yes, it's gnocchi.

1566
01:15:14,010 --> 01:15:14,777
Who made it?

1567
01:15:14,777 --> 01:15:16,779
- Jong Eun did.
- Jong Eun?

1568
01:15:17,280 --> 01:15:19,849
It really looks restaurant-quality.

1569
01:15:19,849 --> 01:15:20,917
Right?

1570
01:15:20,917 --> 01:15:22,285
It really does.

1571
01:15:23,286 --> 01:15:25,688
This is the vitamin drink.

1572
01:15:25,688 --> 01:15:26,890
Really?

1573
01:15:26,890 --> 01:15:27,957
I'd like some.

1574
01:15:27,957 --> 01:15:29,259
(Do Gon hands his tumbler to Ro Bin.)

1575
01:15:29,826 --> 01:15:32,495
(Earlier, on today's date)

1576
01:15:32,929 --> 01:15:36,533
I mixed vitamins into some water too.

1577
01:15:36,533 --> 01:15:37,834
Into water?

1578
01:15:37,834 --> 01:15:39,035
Vitamin water.

1579
01:15:39,035 --> 01:15:40,670
I left it in the car.

1580
01:15:40,670 --> 01:15:41,838
Darn it.

1581
01:15:42,472 --> 01:15:43,506
Darn it.

1582
01:15:43,506 --> 01:15:46,476
You seemed tired yesterday,

1583
01:15:46,476 --> 01:15:49,345
so I thought it'd help while we were out.

1584
01:15:49,345 --> 01:15:50,580
I'm all right.

1585
01:15:51,848 --> 01:15:56,219
I'd planned to give it to Ro Bin.

1586
01:15:56,219 --> 01:16:00,823
I mixed it this morning and took it out,

1587
01:16:00,823 --> 01:16:02,192
but I left it in my car.

1588
01:16:02,859 --> 01:16:06,196
(Do Gon's thoughtful gesture
didn't reach Ro Bin.)

1589
01:16:06,496 --> 01:16:09,399
"I should give it to her now."

1590
01:16:09,766 --> 01:16:12,769
He's such a thoughtful person.

1591
01:16:12,769 --> 01:16:16,439
It did make my heart flutter a little.

1592
01:16:17,807 --> 01:16:18,808
Can I drink it now?

1593
01:16:18,808 --> 01:16:20,944
Sure, you can.

1594
01:16:20,944 --> 01:16:23,112
- It's like vitamin water.
- Thank you.

1595
01:16:25,181 --> 01:16:26,716
That's incredible.

1596
01:16:26,716 --> 01:16:28,017
At least it reached her in the end.

1597
01:16:28,017 --> 01:16:30,486
Being with Do Gon would feel so easy.

1598
01:16:30,720 --> 01:16:32,388
I want those two to get together.

1599
01:16:32,388 --> 01:16:33,857
They'd date without any pressure.

1600
01:16:33,857 --> 01:16:35,291
A perfect score.

1601
01:16:35,291 --> 01:16:36,659
That's the best.

1602
01:16:50,173 --> 01:16:52,509
(Peeks around)

1603
01:16:55,445 --> 01:16:59,983
(After dinner, Ro Bin lingers
outside the men's bedroom.)

1604
01:17:04,287 --> 01:17:05,555
(The door opens.)

1605
01:17:05,889 --> 01:17:07,624
There you are. I was looking for you.

1606
01:17:07,624 --> 01:17:08,424
Why?

1607
01:17:08,424 --> 01:17:09,959
Are you going to bed?

1608
01:17:09,959 --> 01:17:11,461
- No.
- You're not?

1609
01:17:11,461 --> 01:17:13,530
Do you want to talk?

1610
01:17:13,530 --> 01:17:15,031
- Now?
- Yeah.

1611
01:17:15,031 --> 01:17:16,232
You can sleep if you're tired.

1612
01:17:16,232 --> 01:17:17,433
No, I'm not tired.

1613
01:17:19,235 --> 01:17:22,005
Aren't you cold? I'm not cold either.

1614
01:17:23,273 --> 01:17:24,340
It's just...

1615
01:17:24,340 --> 01:17:25,708
What is it?

1616
01:17:26,543 --> 01:17:28,978
- Today...
- What is it?

1617
01:17:28,978 --> 01:17:29,979
What about today?

1618
01:17:30,613 --> 01:17:32,615
Earlier today, I...

1619
01:17:32,615 --> 01:17:35,185
I wanted to talk too.

1620
01:17:37,654 --> 01:17:38,855
Come over here and sit down.

1621
01:17:41,925 --> 01:17:42,992
I'm sorry about today.

1622
01:17:42,992 --> 01:17:44,194
Why?

1623
01:17:44,194 --> 01:17:47,130
I didn't expect weather like this.

1624
01:17:47,130 --> 01:17:48,798
You have nothing to apologize for.

1625
01:17:48,798 --> 01:17:51,467
You said your throat hurt
after we got back.

1626
01:17:51,467 --> 01:17:52,435
No.

1627
01:17:52,435 --> 01:17:55,004
I worried the cold air made you sick
because of me.

1628
01:17:55,004 --> 01:17:56,206
That's really not it.

1629
01:17:56,206 --> 01:17:57,807
It really isn't.

1630
01:17:57,807 --> 01:18:00,343
That's not what happened.

1631
01:18:00,343 --> 01:18:03,112
When we were driving home,

1632
01:18:03,112 --> 01:18:07,984
I said, "There might be many things...

1633
01:18:07,984 --> 01:18:10,019
I'd have to accommodate."

1634
01:18:11,554 --> 01:18:15,058
But I think I spoke too soon...

1635
01:18:15,058 --> 01:18:16,392
about all of that.

1636
01:18:19,562 --> 01:18:21,598
I think I was scared too.

1637
01:18:22,765 --> 01:18:24,901
Without realizing it,

1638
01:18:25,602 --> 01:18:26,903
I think I hurt you, Ryun Gi.

1639
01:18:28,571 --> 01:18:29,572
I'm sorry.

1640
01:18:30,673 --> 01:18:32,242
(Right after the date)

1641
01:18:33,042 --> 01:18:36,145
Honestly, you're still going through it.

1642
01:18:36,145 --> 01:18:37,280
Right.

1643
01:18:37,280 --> 01:18:39,415
When I thought about that,

1644
01:18:39,415 --> 01:18:41,651
I had so much on my mind.

1645
01:18:41,651 --> 01:18:43,953
I felt I needed more time to think.

1646
01:18:45,755 --> 01:18:49,125
Ever since my battle with illness,

1647
01:18:49,125 --> 01:18:50,727
I've wanted anyone looking at me...

1648
01:18:50,727 --> 01:18:53,496
to see me without prejudice.

1649
01:18:53,496 --> 01:18:57,100
But I realized I was judging him that way.

1650
01:18:58,501 --> 01:19:01,137
I think that's why I kept feeling sorry.

1651
01:19:01,137 --> 01:19:04,073
I wondered why I'd said that so suddenly.

1652
01:19:04,073 --> 01:19:06,042
I felt bad about it.

1653
01:19:07,877 --> 01:19:11,814
I understood why you said it.

1654
01:19:11,814 --> 01:19:14,817
When I heard it earlier,

1655
01:19:19,055 --> 01:19:20,590
to be really honest,

1656
01:19:21,858 --> 01:19:24,994
the person on my first date here...

1657
01:19:24,994 --> 01:19:28,498
voiced my biggest concern.

1658
01:19:28,498 --> 01:19:29,666
So...

1659
01:19:30,266 --> 01:19:34,838
what I'd feared suddenly felt real,

1660
01:19:35,605 --> 01:19:39,309
and it felt like a wall between us.

1661
01:19:39,309 --> 01:19:41,077
Yes, it must have.

1662
01:19:41,644 --> 01:19:43,813
Of course you'd want to date
someone healthy.

1663
01:19:44,781 --> 01:19:47,083
I think that's completely natural.

1664
01:19:47,884 --> 01:19:50,253
So please don't feel too bad about it.

1665
01:19:50,253 --> 01:19:53,456
I came here thinking the exact same thing.

1666
01:19:54,390 --> 01:19:55,859
I think I was just...

1667
01:19:56,926 --> 01:19:58,261
too afraid.

1668
01:19:59,596 --> 01:20:02,232
I was scared and worried too much.

1669
01:20:03,266 --> 01:20:04,968
I completely understand.

1670
01:20:04,968 --> 01:20:07,837
You had the very same concern I did.

1671
01:20:09,072 --> 01:20:11,774
Please don't feel too sorry.

1672
01:20:14,677 --> 01:20:16,246
(Ryun Gi eases Ro Bin's guilt.)

1673
01:20:16,246 --> 01:20:19,315
I think it's completely natural
to feel that way.

1674
01:20:20,950 --> 01:20:22,585
I'm...

1675
01:20:22,585 --> 01:20:24,220
not that fragile.

1676
01:20:24,220 --> 01:20:26,456
You don't look fragile.

1677
01:20:26,456 --> 01:20:27,991
You really don't.

1678
01:20:30,727 --> 01:20:33,029
You just seemed so cautious around me.

1679
01:20:33,029 --> 01:20:35,698
Yes, you're right. It was on my mind.

1680
01:20:37,267 --> 01:20:39,202
Don't take it too much to heart.

1681
01:20:43,940 --> 01:20:47,911
(They understand each other
without needing many words.)

1682
01:20:50,647 --> 01:20:52,115
I honestly thought...

1683
01:20:52,115 --> 01:20:54,384
there was nothing to apologize for.

1684
01:20:54,384 --> 01:20:57,153
I was grateful that she apologized,

1685
01:20:57,153 --> 01:20:59,155
because that took courage too.

1686
01:20:59,155 --> 01:21:02,659
It confirmed what I'd thought about her.

1687
01:21:02,659 --> 01:21:06,196
She's truly thoughtful and considerate.

1688
01:21:06,196 --> 01:21:09,165
I was grateful for her honesty.

1689
01:21:13,736 --> 01:21:16,339
(Amid the swirl of emotions,)

1690
01:21:17,707 --> 01:21:21,177
(the Room of Time opens on Day 2.)

1691
01:21:21,544 --> 01:21:22,612
(The Room of Time finally opens again.)

1692
01:21:22,612 --> 01:21:24,080
- Finally.
- It's open.

1693
01:21:24,914 --> 01:21:26,449
I'm dying to know.

1694
01:21:26,616 --> 01:21:27,717
(Bursts out laughing)

1695
01:21:28,985 --> 01:21:30,787
It's the second night in the Room of Time.

1696
01:21:30,787 --> 01:21:31,521
Exactly.

1697
01:21:31,521 --> 01:21:33,990
- I wonder what changed.
- Right.

1698
01:21:33,990 --> 01:21:35,592
A lot must have changed, right?

1699
01:21:35,592 --> 01:21:37,126
I think it did. For now,

1700
01:21:37,126 --> 01:21:39,329
I'm most curious about Seon Ho's feelings.

1701
01:21:40,296 --> 01:21:41,564
I'm curious about Ro Bin too.

1702
01:21:41,564 --> 01:21:43,800
With Ro Bin's personality,

1703
01:21:43,800 --> 01:21:46,035
I doubt her feelings will spike at once.

1704
01:21:46,035 --> 01:21:47,237
I think they'll build slowly.

1705
01:21:47,237 --> 01:21:49,072
Please don't cut it off halfway this time.

1706
01:21:49,072 --> 01:21:49,939
Seriously.

1707
01:21:50,540 --> 01:21:54,210
(The Room of Time, Day 2,
How have their feelings changed?)

1708
01:21:54,577 --> 01:21:58,815
(Who will Na Young choose tonight?)

1709
01:22:05,188 --> 01:22:08,658
I haven't spoken with Do Gon even once.

1710
01:22:10,059 --> 01:22:12,128
I definitely want to talk to him.

1711
01:22:12,962 --> 01:22:15,999
Maybe we'll discover unexpected sides...

1712
01:22:16,399 --> 01:22:17,467
if we talk one-on-one.

1713
01:22:19,302 --> 01:22:23,506
(Na Young - 100 minutes - Do Gon)

1714
01:22:24,007 --> 01:22:29,512
(100 minutes,
Kim Na Young and Han Do Gon matched.)

1715
01:22:30,513 --> 01:22:35,518
(Where will Jong Eun's time go?)

1716
01:22:40,456 --> 01:22:44,561
(Kang Min Young)

1717
01:22:44,561 --> 01:22:48,131
I had so much fun talking to Min Young...

1718
01:22:48,131 --> 01:22:49,999
and spending time with her.

1719
01:22:52,235 --> 01:22:53,469
Try it.

1720
01:22:54,504 --> 01:22:55,471
Just a tiny bit.

1721
01:22:56,539 --> 01:22:57,473
Bite it.

1722
01:22:57,473 --> 01:22:58,541
No.

1723
01:22:59,142 --> 01:23:00,476
How is it?

1724
01:23:01,845 --> 01:23:02,712
(His fun one-on-one time with Min Young)

1725
01:23:02,712 --> 01:23:03,913
Don't eat it again.

1726
01:23:03,913 --> 01:23:05,315
I didn't know you hated it that much.

1727
01:23:06,449 --> 01:23:08,651
I wanted to go on a date with her,

1728
01:23:08,651 --> 01:23:10,820
so I gave her all 100 minutes.

1729
01:23:10,820 --> 01:23:12,255
(Jong Eun - 100 minutes - Min Young)

1730
01:23:12,755 --> 01:23:18,261
(100 minutes,
Kang Min Young and Kim Jong Eun matched.)

1731
01:23:19,495 --> 01:23:23,233
(How does Min Young feel right now?)

1732
01:23:27,804 --> 01:23:30,240
(Kim Seon Ho)

1733
01:23:30,240 --> 01:23:31,174
(Presses firmly)

1734
01:23:33,576 --> 01:23:35,678
We went shopping together today...

1735
01:23:35,678 --> 01:23:37,480
and got to talk a little.

1736
01:23:39,382 --> 01:23:41,985
I'm becoming more curious about him.

1737
01:23:43,720 --> 01:23:45,488
I realized I must see Seon Ho...

1738
01:23:45,488 --> 01:23:47,056
as a potential partner.

1739
01:23:47,056 --> 01:23:49,459
I need to go on a date with him.

1740
01:23:49,893 --> 01:23:54,097
(Min Young - 100 minutes - Seon Ho)

1741
01:23:54,631 --> 01:24:00,103
(100 minutes,
Kim Seon Ho and Kang Min Young matched.)

1742
01:24:00,403 --> 01:24:01,337
(A 100-minute party)

1743
01:24:01,337 --> 01:24:02,338
Now they're all...

1744
01:24:02,338 --> 01:24:03,373
This is huge.

1745
01:24:03,373 --> 01:24:04,607
They've figured it out.

1746
01:24:04,607 --> 01:24:06,376
They can't do this halfway.

1747
01:24:06,376 --> 01:24:07,744
If they really like someone...

1748
01:24:07,744 --> 01:24:09,245
and truly want to meet them,

1749
01:24:09,245 --> 01:24:10,780
they have to go all in.

1750
01:24:10,780 --> 01:24:12,148
That's what they've realized.

1751
01:24:12,148 --> 01:24:13,383
What will Ye Ji do?

1752
01:24:13,383 --> 01:24:15,118
Sorry, I got way too into it.

1753
01:24:18,121 --> 01:24:21,357
(Ye Ji enters the Room of Time.)

1754
01:24:23,793 --> 01:24:26,462
My date with Seon Ho...

1755
01:24:26,462 --> 01:24:28,965
made such a strong impression on me.

1756
01:24:28,965 --> 01:24:35,004
I wondered if I could feel this much...

1757
01:24:35,004 --> 01:24:36,639
after just one date.

1758
01:24:36,873 --> 01:24:38,775
(Earlier, on today's date)

1759
01:24:38,775 --> 01:24:41,110
But I think...

1760
01:24:41,110 --> 01:24:43,112
you're the person I know, Ye Ji.

1761
01:24:44,280 --> 01:24:46,616
What? What do you mean?

1762
01:24:46,616 --> 01:24:49,285
I think we've followed each other's blogs.

1763
01:24:49,285 --> 01:24:51,521
- What? Really?
- Yes.

1764
01:24:51,521 --> 01:24:53,890
I'd even read your recent updates.

1765
01:24:54,390 --> 01:24:57,927
Yesterday, I wasn't sure it was you.

1766
01:24:57,927 --> 01:24:59,128
Really?

1767
01:24:59,128 --> 01:25:01,698
I was surprised and fascinated,

1768
01:25:01,698 --> 01:25:03,533
and it made my heart flutter.

1769
01:25:03,533 --> 01:25:06,669
It felt like something out of a movie.

1770
01:25:13,843 --> 01:25:17,413
(Her time heads toward Seon Ho.)

1771
01:25:21,718 --> 01:25:23,319
(Hesitates)

1772
01:25:29,659 --> 01:25:33,129
(The time stops at 50 minutes.)

1773
01:25:33,129 --> 01:25:34,497
- What?
- Fifty minutes?

1774
01:25:35,532 --> 01:25:36,966
Did it stop halfway?

1775
01:25:36,966 --> 01:25:38,801
Seriously?

1776
01:25:43,406 --> 01:25:46,543
I was already torn before going in.

1777
01:25:46,876 --> 01:25:49,746
After coming back from the date,

1778
01:25:50,280 --> 01:25:51,981
things felt uncertain again.

1779
01:25:54,984 --> 01:25:56,186
Enjoy your meal.

1780
01:26:01,257 --> 01:26:02,458
That was so cold.

1781
01:26:02,458 --> 01:26:03,860
- That was too cold.
- There's no way...

1782
01:26:03,860 --> 01:26:05,428
Honestly, that was a little too much.

1783
01:26:05,428 --> 01:26:07,864
I don't think he meant to seem cold.

1784
01:26:07,864 --> 01:26:09,666
But that was so cold.

1785
01:26:09,666 --> 01:26:11,167
They need to reshoot that scene.

1786
01:26:11,167 --> 01:26:11,968
Seriously.

1787
01:26:11,968 --> 01:26:14,237
- That was a blooper.
- They need a retake.

1788
01:26:15,772 --> 01:26:16,873
Enjoy your meal.

1789
01:26:17,407 --> 01:26:21,311
But seeing him respond like that,

1790
01:26:21,311 --> 01:26:25,882
I thought he might want
to meet other people.

1791
01:26:26,616 --> 01:26:30,086
Giving him all my time felt like
I'd deny him that chance.

1792
01:26:30,086 --> 01:26:31,888
So I agonized.

1793
01:26:35,992 --> 01:26:39,495
(Where Ye Ji's time goes)

1794
01:26:43,666 --> 01:26:46,503
(Ye Ji - 50 minutes - Seon Ho)

1795
01:26:46,503 --> 01:26:49,305
(Ye Ji - 50 minutes - Do Gon)

1796
01:26:54,377 --> 01:26:55,945
Well...

1797
01:26:59,649 --> 01:27:03,520
(How does Seon Ho feel right now?)

1798
01:27:04,063 --> 01:27:06,399
I definitely enjoyed my date with Ye Ji.

1799
01:27:07,400 --> 01:27:09,068
We already had a connection.

1800
01:27:09,068 --> 01:27:11,838
It was nice to see her,

1801
01:27:11,838 --> 01:27:12,739
and I had fun.

1802
01:27:13,473 --> 01:27:14,908
But I wasn't sure what it meant...

1803
01:27:14,908 --> 01:27:16,910
that I enjoyed being with her.

1804
01:27:16,910 --> 01:27:18,111
That confused me.

1805
01:27:18,645 --> 01:27:22,182
Was I enjoying it romantically?

1806
01:27:22,182 --> 01:27:23,683
Or was it just a sense of familiarity?

1807
01:27:24,551 --> 01:27:27,320
Was it more like that?
That's what I was wondering.

1808
01:27:28,822 --> 01:27:30,523
Seriously?

1809
01:27:30,523 --> 01:27:32,158
But he stirred up her feelings.

1810
01:27:32,158 --> 01:27:33,593
That's not right.

1811
01:27:33,593 --> 01:27:35,228
- I agree.
- Right?

1812
01:27:36,930 --> 01:27:39,365
(Contemplates)

1813
01:27:51,911 --> 01:27:56,282
(Seo Ro Bin)

1814
01:27:56,950 --> 01:27:58,251
(Startled)

1815
01:27:58,251 --> 01:27:59,519
Ro Bin?

1816
01:28:03,189 --> 01:28:04,124
What?

1817
01:28:04,124 --> 01:28:05,091
My goodness.

1818
01:28:05,091 --> 01:28:06,860
What is going on?

1819
01:28:07,861 --> 01:28:10,430
I'd quit the show right then.

1820
01:28:10,430 --> 01:28:11,865
"I'm too stressed out. I can't do this."

1821
01:28:13,032 --> 01:28:14,901
- "My head hurts."
- "My head hurts."

1822
01:28:23,076 --> 01:28:24,010
(Jung Ye Ji)

1823
01:28:32,385 --> 01:28:33,653
Just like yesterday,

1824
01:28:33,653 --> 01:28:36,523
I gave Ro Bin and Ye Ji 50 minutes each.

1825
01:28:37,056 --> 01:28:40,293
I haven't talked to Ro Bin yet,

1826
01:28:40,293 --> 01:28:42,095
so I'm still curious about her.

1827
01:28:42,095 --> 01:28:45,832
I want to get
to know everyone carefully...

1828
01:28:45,832 --> 01:28:47,500
before I make up my mind.

1829
01:28:48,868 --> 01:28:54,340
(100 minutes,
Jung Ye Ji and Kim Seon Ho matched.)

1830
01:28:55,542 --> 01:28:59,512
(Ryun Gi enters the Room of Time.)

1831
01:29:03,483 --> 01:29:05,919
Well...

1832
01:29:16,162 --> 01:29:19,365
My thoughts are a complicated mess
right now.

1833
01:29:19,365 --> 01:29:20,467
I guess...

1834
01:29:20,467 --> 01:29:21,968
it's only human...

1835
01:29:21,968 --> 01:29:25,472
to want to date...

1836
01:29:25,472 --> 01:29:26,773
someone healthy.

1837
01:29:26,773 --> 01:29:30,910
Her saying, "Those things worried me,"

1838
01:29:30,910 --> 01:29:34,113
has really stayed with me.

1839
01:29:36,249 --> 01:29:41,387
(He hesitates before his choice.)

1840
01:29:55,368 --> 01:30:01,307
(After agonizing,
he gives Ro Bin more time.)

1841
01:30:14,254 --> 01:30:17,157
To ease some of that pressure,

1842
01:30:17,157 --> 01:30:20,727
I gave her 70 minutes, less than before.

1843
01:30:27,100 --> 01:30:28,968
If...

1844
01:30:28,968 --> 01:30:31,838
we get matched again tomorrow,

1845
01:30:32,305 --> 01:30:33,940
that would mean...

1846
01:30:34,974 --> 01:30:37,243
she gave me 30 minutes,
which is more than 10.

1847
01:30:37,977 --> 01:30:40,046
That could be a hopeful sign.

1848
01:30:42,248 --> 01:30:43,950
Giving Ro Bin too much time...

1849
01:30:43,950 --> 01:30:46,453
might also feel like pressure to her.

1850
01:30:46,453 --> 01:30:48,354
But he can't hide his feelings completely.

1851
01:30:48,354 --> 01:30:49,255
Right.

1852
01:30:49,255 --> 01:30:52,192
This is such a real-life dilemma.

1853
01:30:52,192 --> 01:30:54,894
But he can't pick someone he doesn't like.

1854
01:30:54,894 --> 01:30:56,129
Ryun Gi is amazing.

1855
01:30:56,129 --> 01:30:57,764
- He is.
- Seriously.

1856
01:30:59,833 --> 01:31:04,504
(The time he couldn't bring himself
to give Ro Bin)

1857
01:31:04,504 --> 01:31:08,441
(Kim Na Young)

1858
01:31:08,741 --> 01:31:12,345
(Ryun Gi - 30 minutes - Na Young)

1859
01:31:12,345 --> 01:31:15,915
(Ryun Gi - 70 minutes - Ro Bin)

1860
01:31:29,562 --> 01:31:35,335
(Seo Ro Bin)

1861
01:31:36,402 --> 01:31:41,508
(Do Gon makes his choice
without hesitation.)

1862
01:31:42,775 --> 01:31:44,744
(Grins)

1863
01:31:48,481 --> 01:31:50,416
The date felt shorter than I expected.

1864
01:31:50,416 --> 01:31:51,951
I wished we'd had more time.

1865
01:31:52,252 --> 01:31:57,123
(His first date with Ro Bin)

1866
01:31:57,490 --> 01:31:58,358
There.

1867
01:31:58,358 --> 01:32:01,027
I just wanted to learn more about Ro Bin.

1868
01:32:07,200 --> 01:32:08,201
(Push)

1869
01:32:10,537 --> 01:32:13,306
I gave all 100 of my minutes to Ro Bin.

1870
01:32:15,308 --> 01:32:16,676
(Unbelievable)

1871
01:32:17,710 --> 01:32:19,045
Hundred Do Gon.

1872
01:32:19,045 --> 01:32:20,346
Hundred Do Gon.

1873
01:32:20,346 --> 01:32:21,614
Seriously.

1874
01:32:21,614 --> 01:32:23,149
My gosh.

1875
01:32:23,149 --> 01:32:24,384
Hundred Do Gon.

1876
01:32:24,384 --> 01:32:25,919
Do Gon is unbelievable.

1877
01:32:25,919 --> 01:32:26,820
Do Gon really is Hundred Do Gon.

1878
01:32:26,820 --> 01:32:28,087
He must've loved the date.

1879
01:32:28,087 --> 01:32:29,456
He's number one.

1880
01:32:29,456 --> 01:32:30,857
He's the best.

1881
01:32:31,791 --> 01:32:34,194
If Ro Bin also gives him 100 minutes,

1882
01:32:34,194 --> 01:32:35,495
won't that make 200 minutes?

1883
01:32:35,495 --> 01:32:36,930
My gosh.

1884
01:32:40,066 --> 01:32:46,539
(Once again, Do Gon gives
all his time to Ro Bin.)

1885
01:32:48,741 --> 01:32:54,447
(Do Gon - 100 minutes - Ro Bin)

1886
01:32:54,614 --> 01:33:00,453
(100 minutes,
Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon matched.)

1887
01:33:07,794 --> 01:33:09,696
I had fun with Ryun Gi.

1888
01:33:13,666 --> 01:33:15,969
I found him a little cute too,

1889
01:33:15,969 --> 01:33:18,404
and the way he talked was endearing.

1890
01:33:18,404 --> 01:33:19,739
He had a teasing charm...

1891
01:33:19,739 --> 01:33:23,343
and knew how to lead the conversation.

1892
01:33:23,877 --> 01:33:26,479
I could tell he was a wonderful person.

1893
01:33:30,450 --> 01:33:32,185
I completely understand.

1894
01:33:32,185 --> 01:33:34,988
You had the very same concern I did.

1895
01:33:36,723 --> 01:33:38,558
Don't take it too much to heart.

1896
01:33:39,559 --> 01:33:40,994
When he said that,

1897
01:33:40,994 --> 01:33:43,963
I thought it was incredibly admirable.

1898
01:33:43,963 --> 01:33:45,865
I was so grateful.

1899
01:33:46,366 --> 01:33:47,600
I truly was.

1900
01:33:47,934 --> 01:33:51,204
- Is rolling up the sleeves better?
- Yes, it is.

1901
01:33:51,204 --> 01:33:52,505
- How much should I...
- Not too much.

1902
01:33:54,741 --> 01:33:58,311
He also seemed to be trying hard...

1903
01:33:58,311 --> 01:34:00,947
to show me that he was interested.

1904
01:34:00,947 --> 01:34:03,850
He kept expressing it in subtle ways.

1905
01:34:03,850 --> 01:34:06,986
It wasn't overwhelming. I really liked it.

1906
01:34:06,986 --> 01:34:09,722
If I were to date someone,

1907
01:34:09,722 --> 01:34:12,859
I'd want to date someone like Do Gon.

1908
01:34:13,393 --> 01:34:14,427
But...

1909
01:34:20,667 --> 01:34:21,835
What?

1910
01:34:21,835 --> 01:34:23,703
"But?" Why?

1911
01:34:23,703 --> 01:34:24,771
What is it?

1912
01:34:25,405 --> 01:34:28,641
Seon Ho?

1913
01:34:28,641 --> 01:34:29,742
Wait a minute.

1914
01:34:35,448 --> 01:34:37,517
But right now,

1915
01:34:37,517 --> 01:34:38,918
I just...

1916
01:34:38,918 --> 01:34:40,353
Right now, this...

1917
01:34:40,353 --> 01:34:42,255
Something's wrong with me right now.

1918
01:34:42,922 --> 01:34:44,557
I don't know.

1919
01:34:45,725 --> 01:34:48,661
(Why Ro Bin struggles with her choice)

1920
01:34:49,295 --> 01:34:53,733
(Who will receive Ro Bin's time?)

1921
01:35:03,576 --> 01:35:05,278
I just...

1922
01:35:06,212 --> 01:35:08,014
I never thought I'd feel this way either.

1923
01:35:12,385 --> 01:35:16,356
(After agonizing,
Ro Bin sends her time to someone.)

1924
01:35:25,498 --> 01:35:27,767
(After agonizing,
Ro Bin uses all 100 minutes.)

1925
01:35:27,767 --> 01:35:29,536
She used all 100 minutes.

1926
01:35:29,536 --> 01:35:31,070
They'd better not end it here.

1927
01:35:31,871 --> 01:35:33,206
I won't forgive them.

1928
01:35:33,206 --> 01:35:34,140
Seriously.

1929
01:35:34,140 --> 01:35:36,142
Don't leave.

1930
01:35:36,943 --> 01:35:41,014
(What choice did Ro Bin make
that shocked everyone?)

1931
01:35:42,348 --> 01:35:43,750
Really?

1932
01:35:43,750 --> 01:35:44,851
Wait.

1933
01:35:44,851 --> 01:35:46,453
(Startled)

1934
01:35:48,121 --> 01:35:52,058
(Ro Bin - 100 minutes - Jong Eun)

1935
01:35:52,058 --> 01:35:56,896
(Kim Jong Eun)

1936
01:35:58,031 --> 01:36:02,702
(Love Against Time)

1937
01:36:03,069 --> 01:36:04,137
My goodness.

1938
01:36:04,137 --> 01:36:05,138
My heart fluttered.

1939
01:36:05,138 --> 01:36:08,475
I earned it by giving all of my time.

1940
01:36:08,475 --> 01:36:09,309
I was curious.

1941
01:36:09,309 --> 01:36:10,610
Now you've piqued my curiosity.

1942
01:36:10,610 --> 01:36:12,378
What?

1943
01:36:12,378 --> 01:36:14,681
He felt like such a mature man.

1944
01:36:14,681 --> 01:36:15,715
You're very handsome.

1945
01:36:15,715 --> 01:36:17,317
Is there anything you want to ask me?

1946
01:36:17,317 --> 01:36:18,518
I thought you were upset.

1947
01:36:18,518 --> 01:36:20,753
She isn't interested in me.

1948
01:36:20,753 --> 01:36:21,855
They're not on the same wavelength.

1949
01:36:21,855 --> 01:36:23,456
It feels like
they keep missing each other.

1950
01:36:23,456 --> 01:36:24,624
What? What is it?

1951
01:36:24,624 --> 01:36:25,658
You're checking the time?

1952
01:36:25,658 --> 01:36:26,993
Let's get going.

1953
01:36:26,993 --> 01:36:29,195
Today feels unusually long.

1954
01:36:29,195 --> 01:36:31,131
He must be interested in someone.

1955
01:36:31,998 --> 01:36:33,066
What?

1956
01:36:33,066 --> 01:36:34,267
Love is hard.

1957
01:36:34,267 --> 01:36:35,535
What do you think of me?

1958
01:36:35,535 --> 01:36:36,469
I really liked it.

1959
01:36:36,469 --> 01:36:37,804
Do you flirt pretty openly?

1960
01:36:37,804 --> 01:36:38,605
Yes.

1961
01:36:38,605 --> 01:36:40,206
- No.
- My goodness.

1962
01:36:40,206 --> 01:36:41,841
It's neck and neck.

1963
